  FT["MY-H4742"] = {"id":"MY-H4742","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2012&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2012年民用航空（修正）条例","en":"CIVIL AVIATION (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2012","orig":"CIVIL AVIATION (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2012","ms":"Peraturan Penerbangan Awam (Pindaan) 2012","vi":"Quy định về Hàng không dân dụng (Sửa đổi) năm 2012","th":"ข้อบังคับการบินพลเรือน (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2012","id":"Peraturan Penerbangan Sipil (Perubahan) Tahun 2012"},"level":"regulation","category":"03_涉外投资与贸易","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2012","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\03_涉外投资与贸易\\2012_P.U.(A)344-2012_CIVIL AVIATION (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2012.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4742-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1.  (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\nPenerbangan Awam (Pindaan) 2012.\n\n (2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini  mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 November 2012.\n\nPindaan Jadual Kedua Belas"}},{"id":"MY-H4742-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2.  Peraturan-Peraturan Penerbangan Awam 1996 [ P.U. (A) 139/1996 ] dipinda\ndalam Jadual Kedua Belas di bawah kepala \"Bahagian B\", dengan menggantikan\nperenggan 23 dengan perenggan yang berikut:\n\n             \"23. Pas Lapangan Terbang\n\n(1)   Seseorang p emohon bagi pas lapangan terbang  hendaklah\nmembayar kepada syarikat berlesen caj yang berikut:\n\n                                Kategori pas Caj\n   Pas tetap lapangan terbang (dua tahun)\n\nRM25.00\n   Pas sementara lapangan terbang (satu tahun)\n\nRM20.00\n   Pas pelawat lapangan terbang (enam bulan)\n\nRM17.00\n   Pas harian lapangan terbang (satu hari)\n\n        RM2.00\n\n(2)   Bagi maksud menggantikan mana -mana pas lapangan terbang\nyang hilang, pemohon pas lapangan terbang itu hendaklah membayar kepada\n\nsyarikat berlesen caj yang berikut sebagai tambahan kepada caj yang kena\ndibayar di bawah subperenggan (1):\n\nDibuat 11 Oktober 2012\n[KP/PUU/0.440/W/BU/2; PN(PU2)38/VII]\n\n      DATO' SERI KONG CHO HA\n                  Menteri Pengangkutan\n\nUlangan kehilangan Caj\n   Kehilangan kali pertama\n\nRM50.00\n   Kehilangan kali kedua\n\nRM80.00\n   Kehilangan kali ketiga dan yang kemudiannya\n\n     RM100.00\".\n\nCIVIL AVIATION ACT 1969\n\nCIVIL AVIATION (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2012\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 3 of the Civil Aviation Act 1969 [ Act 3],\nthe Minister makes the following regulations:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4743"] = {"id":"MY-H4743","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2013&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2013年关税（计价）（原油）（第24号）令","en":"CUSTOMS (VALUES) (CRUDE PETROLEUM OIL) (NO. 24) ORDER 2013","orig":"CUSTOMS (VALUES) (CRUDE PETROLEUM OIL) (NO. 24) ORDER 2013","ms":"Perintah Kastam (Nilai) (Minyak Mentah Petroleum) (Bilangan 24) 2013","vi":"Lệnh về Hải quan (Trị giá) (Dầu thô) (số 24) năm 2013","th":"คำสั่งศุลกากร (มูลค่า) (น้ำมันดิบ) (ฉบับที่ 24) ค.ศ. 2013","id":"Perintah Kepabeanan (Nilai) (Minyak Bumi Mentah) (Nomor 24) Tahun 2013"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2013","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2013_P.U.(A)344-2013_CUSTOMS (VALUES) (CRUDE PETROLEUM OIL) (NO. 24) ORDER 2013.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4743-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Kastam (Nilai -Nilai)\n(Minyak Mentah Petroleum)  (No. 24) 2013  dan  hendaklah  mula  berkuat kuasa\nbagi tempoh dari 28 November 2013 hingga 11 Disember 2013.\n\nPemungutan dan pembayaran duti kastam"}},{"id":"MY-H4743-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Bagi maksud pemungutan dan pembayaran duti -duti kastam, menurut\nperuntukan-peruntukan Perintah Duti Kastam 2007 [ P.U. (A) 441/2007 ], nilai  bagi\ntiap-tiap satu barang berduti yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (1) dan (2) Jadual mengikut\nunitnya yang tersebut dalam ruang (3) hendaklah nilai yang dinyatakan dalam\nruang (4).\n\nCUSTOMS ACT 1967\n\nCUSTOMS (VALUES) (CRUDE PETROLEUM OIL) (NO. 24) ORDER  2013\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 12 of the Customs Act 1967 [Act 235 ],\nthe Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\nJADUAL/SCHEDULE\n\nBarang\n(Goods)\n(1)\n\nSubkepala\n(Subheading)\n(2)\nUnit\n(Unit)\n(3)\nNilai\n(Value)\n(4)\n\nTapis Blend  2709.00.100 per barrel RM367.31\nLabuan Crude 2709.00.100 per barrel RM371.41\nMiri Light Crude 2709.00.100 per barrel RM370.46\nDulang  2709.00.100 per barrel RM368.57\nBintulu Crude                              2709.00.100 per barrel RM366.37\nTerengganu Condensate 2709.00.900 per barrel RM343.36\nBintulu Condensate 2709.00.900 per barrel RM344.30\nMasa   2709.00.100 per barrel RM217.03\nAsam Paya  2709.00.100 per barrel RM371.57\nKidurong 2709.00.100 per barrel RM366.68\nPenara Blend 2709.00.100 per barrel RM362.58\nMinyak Mentah Fairley\nBaram\n2709.00.100 per barrel RM230.90\nCakerawala Condensate 2709.00.900 per barrel RM337.18\nAngsi Crude  2709.00.100 per barrel RM375.10\nCendor Crude 2709.00.100 per barrel RM375.82\nAbu Blend                                   2709.00.100 per barrel RM357.70\nKikeh Crude                                2709.00.100 per barrel RM369.93\nBunga Orkid                                2709.00.100 per barrel RM363.84\nBunga Kekwa 2709.00.100 per barrel RM362.58\nMuda Condensate 2709.00.900 per barrel RM356.12\nSepat\nBerantai\n2709.00.100\n2709.00.100\nper barrel\nper barrel\nRM369.83\nRM344.46\n\nDibuat  22 November 2013\nMade  22 November 2013\n[KE. HT(94)819/01-1/Klt. 14/(5); R.9003/54Z-40; PN(PU2)338/XXX]\n\nDengan arahan Menteri Kewangan/\n              By direction of the Minister of Finance\n\n    Bagi pihak dan atas nama Menteri Kewangan/\n          On behalf and in the name of the Minister of Finance\n\n DATO' SITI HALIMAH BINTI ISMAIL\n  Setiausaha/\nUnder Secretary\nBahagian Analisa Cukai/\nTax Analysis Division"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4744"] = {"id":"MY-H4744","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2014&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2014年联邦道路（私营管理）（通行费征收）（吉隆坡—雪兰莪大道）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KL-KUALA-SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY) ORDER 2014","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KL-KUALA-SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY) ORDER 2014","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Pengurusan Swasta) (Kutipan Tol) (Lebuhraya KL-Kuala Selangor) 2014","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Quản lý tư nhân) (Thu phí đường bộ) (Đường cao tốc KL-Kuala Selangor) năm 2014","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (การบริหารจัดการเอกชน) (การจัดเก็บค่าผ่านทาง) (ทางด่วน KL-กัวลาสลังงอร์) ค.ศ. 2014","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Pengelolaan Swasta) (Pemungutan Tol) (Jalan Tol KL-Kuala Selangor) Tahun 2014"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2014","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 5 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2014_P.U.(A)344-2014_FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KL-KUALA-SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY) ORDER 2.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4744-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Jalan-Jalan Persekutuan\n\n(Pengurusan Persendirian) (Pungutan Tol) (Lebuh Raya KL-Kuala Selangor)\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 Januari 2015.\n\nPemberikuasaan untuk memungut tol"}},{"id":"MY-H4744-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. (1) KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway Berhad diberi kuasa bagi tempoh dari\n\n1 Januari 2015 hingga 28 Oktober 2048 untuk meminta, memungut dan menyimpan tol\n\nyang berkenaan seperti yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (2) Jadual Pertama bagi\n\npenggunaan ke mana-mana arah mana-mana bahagian jalan yang dikenali sebagai\n\nLebuh Raya KL-Kuala Selangor yang bermula dari kilometer 0.00 di koordinat\n\nU 366573.829, T 375376.712 Grid Rectified Skew Orthomorphic (RSO) Geosentrik\n\n(GDM2000) dan berakhir di kilometer 30.70 Lebuh Raya KL-Kuala Selangor\n\ndi koordinat U 364885.563, T 401792.132 Grid RSO Geosentrik (GDM2000)\n\ntermasuklah Persimpangan Bertingkat Ijok, Plaza Tol Ijok, Persimpangan Bertingkat\n\nPuncak Alam, Plaza Tol Kuang Barat, Plaza Tol Kundang Timur, Persimpangan\n\nBertingkat Kundang, Plaza Tol Kundang Barat, Plaza Tol Kuang Timur, Persimpangan\n\nBertingkat Kuang, Plaza Tol Taman Rimba Templer, Persimpangan Bertingkat Taman\n\nRimba Templer dan jalan-jalan sambungannya, iaitu suatu jarak sepanjang\n\n30.70 kilometer oleh kelas kenderaan yang dinyatakan dalam ruang (1) Jadual Pertama.\n\n2. (2) Jalan-jalan yang dinyatakan dalam subperenggan (1) yang bagi\n\npenggunaannya tol dibenarkan diminta, dipungut dan disimpan ditunjukkan dalam peta\n\ndalam Jadual Kedua.\n\nPembayaran Tol"}},{"id":"MY-H4744-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. (1) Tol yang disebut dalam subperenggan 2(1) hendaklah kena dibayar oleh\n\npemandu kenderaan sebelum memasuki Plaza Tol Ijok yang terletak di kilometer 3.72\n\ndi koordinat U 364234.489, T 377608.060 Grid RSO Geosentrik (GDM2000), Plaza Tol\n\nKuang Barat yang terletak di kilometer 13.50 di koordinat U 362137.799, T 386866.042\n\nGrid RSO Geosentrik (GDM2000), Plaza Tol Kundang Timur yang terletak di kilometer\n\n17.05 di koordinat U 362088.978, T 390446.108 Grid RSO Geosentrik (GDM2000),\n\nPlaza Tol Kundang Barat yang terletak di kilometer 18.25 di koordinat U 361892.743,\n\nT 391573.598 Grid RSO Geosentrik (GDM2000), Plaza Tol Kuang Timur yang terletak\n\ndi kilometer 19.60 di koordinat U 361957.886, T 392924.944 Grid RSO Geosentrik\n\n(GDM2000) dan Plaza Tol Taman Rimba Templer yang terletak di kilometer 26.75\n\ndi koordinat U 363934.443, T 398646.808 Grid RSO Geosentrik (GDM2000) di Lebuh\n\nRaya KL-Kuala Selangor, semua jarak diukur dari kilometer 0.00 Lebuh Raya KL-Kuala\n\nSelangor.\n\n(2) Seseorang pemandu kenderaan yang menggunakan suatu kad atau\n\nperanti elektronik hendaklah melalui suatu lorong tol yang mempunyai suatu mesin\n\npembaca kad atau peranti elektronik, menghampiri mesin pembaca itu dan\n\nmenyentuhkan kad atau peranti elektronik ke mesin pembaca itu dan tol yang kena\n\ndibayar hendaklah ditolak daripada kad atau peranti elektronik itu.\n\n(3) Seseorang pemandu kenderaan yang menggunakan tag elektronik\n\nhendaklah, sebelum melalui lorong tag elektronik yang dikhaskan, mempamerkan tag\n\nelektronik atau tag elektronik dengan kad atau peranti elektronik di cermin hadapan\n\nkenderaan dan tol yang kena dibayar hendaklah ditolak daripada tag elektronik atau tag\n\nelektronik dengan kad atau peranti elektronik itu.\n\n(4) \"Kad atau peranti elektronik\" dan \"tag elektronik\" yang disebut dalam\n\nperenggan ini ertinya—\n\n(a) sesuatu kad atau peranti elektronik dan tag elektronik yang\n\ndibenarkan oleh Menteri, yang dikeluarkan bagi maksud\n\npembayaran tol;\n\n(b) berhubung dengan sesuatu kad atau peranti elektronik, suatu kad\n\natau peranti elektronik yang boleh dibaca oleh mesin pembaca\n\nyang dipasang di lorong tol; dan\n\n(c) berhubung dengan sesuatu tag elektronik, suatu tag elektronik\n\nyang boleh menyebabkan palang di lorong tag elektronik yang\n\ndikhaskan dinaikkan secara elektronik.\n\nPengecualian daripada pembayaran tol"}},{"id":"MY-H4744-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. Walau apa pun peruntukan Perintah ini, kenderaan yang dinyatakan dalam\n\nJadual Ketiga dikecualikan daripada pembayaran tol.\n\nPembatalan"}},{"id":"MY-H4744-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. Perintah Jalan-Jalan Persekutuan (Pengurusan Persendirian) (Pungutan Tol)\n\n(Lebuh Raya KL-Kuala Selangor) 2011 [P.U. (A) 263/2011] dibatalkan.\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\n\n[Subperenggan 2(1)]\n\nBAHAGIAN I\n\nKADAR TOL BAGI PLAZA TOL IJOK, PLAZA TOL KUANG BARAT, PLAZA TOL KUANG\n\nTIMUR DAN PLAZA TOL TAMAN RIMBA TEMPLER\n\nDARI 1 JANUARI 2015 HINGGA 28 OKTOBER 2048\n\n( 1 )\n\nKelas Kenderaan\n\n( 2 )\n\nTol Kena Dibayar\n\nRM\n\n1. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan tiga\n\natau empat roda (tidak termasuk teksi dan bas)\n\n2.00\n\n2. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan lima\n\natau enam roda (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n4.00\n\n3. Kenderaan yang mempunyai tiga gandar atau lebih\n\n(tidak termasuk bas)\n\n6.00\n\n4. Teksi 1.00\n\n5. Bas 2.00\n\nBagi maksud mengira bilangan gandar dan roda sesuatu kenderaan, gandar dan roda\n\nmana-mana treler yang ditarik oleh kenderaan itu hendaklah termasuk sebagai\n\nsebahagian daripada gandar dan roda kenderaan itu.\n\nBAHAGIAN II\n\nKADAR TOL BAGI PLAZA TOL KUNDANG TIMUR DAN PLAZA TOL KUNDANG BARAT\n\nDARI 1 JANUARI 2015 HINGGA 28 OKTOBER 2048\n\n( 1 )\n\nKelas Kenderaan\n\n( 2 )\n\nTol Kena Dibayar\n\n RM\n\n1. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan tiga\n\natau empat roda (tidak termasuk teksi dan bas)\n\n1.30\n\n2. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan lima\n\natau enam roda (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n2.60\n\n3. Kenderaan yang mempunyai tiga gandar atau lebih\n\n(tidak termasuk bas)\n\n3.90\n\n4. Teksi 0.70\n\n5. Bas 1.30\n\nBagi maksud mengira bilangan gandar dan roda sesuatu kenderaan, gandar dan roda\n\nmana-mana treler yang ditarik oleh kenderaan itu hendaklah termasuk sebagai\n\nsebahagian daripada gandar dan roda kenderaan itu.\n\nJADUAL KEDUA\n\n[Subperenggan 2(2)]\n\nPETA LEBUH RAYA KL–KUALA SELANGOR\n\nJADUAL KETIGA\n\n[Perenggan 4]\n\nKENDERAAN YANG DIKECUALIKAN\n\n1. Mana-mana kenderaan yang membawa Yang di-Pertuan Agong atau\n\nRaja Permaisuri Agong, Raja-Raja atau Permaisuri-Permaisuri Baginda,\n\nYang di-Pertua Negeri bagi Negeri Melaka, Pulau Pinang, Sabah dan Sarawak\n\natau isteri-isteri mereka, Dato'-Dato' Undang Negeri Sembilan atau Tengku Besar\n\nTampin atau isteri-isteri mereka, Tengku Mahkota atau Raja Muda mana-mana\n\nNegeri atau isteri-isteri mereka, Raja Di-Hilir Perak atau isterinya, atau\n\nmana-mana pembesar asing yang datang melawat.\n\n2. Mana-mana kenderaan Kerajaan yang membawa Perdana Menteri atau Timbalan\n\nPerdana Menteri.\n\n3. Semua kenderaan tentera yang dimiliki oleh Kerajaan atau oleh mana-mana\n\nangkatan pelawat yang ditakrifkan dalam Akta Angkatan Pelawat 1960\n\n[Akta 432].\n\n4. Semua kenderaan Kerajaan yang digunakan semata-mata untuk tugas ambulans,\n\ntugas melawan kebakaran, tugas polis atau tugas menyelamat termasuk\n\nkenderaan pasukan penyelamat daripada Jabatan Pertahanan Awam dan\n\nkenderaan daripada Jabatan Penjara semasa menjalankan tugas mengiringi\n\nbanduan.\n\n5. Semua kenderaan yang bukan kenderaan Kerajaan yang digunakan semata-mata\n\nuntuk tugas ambulans, tugas melawan kebakaran dan tugas menyelamat.\n\n6. Semua motosikal beroda tiga atau beroda empat yang digunakan oleh\n\nmana-mana orang cacat.\n\n7. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan dua roda.\n\nDibuat 17 Disember 2014\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/28; PN(PU2)426/LVI]\n\nDATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\nMenteri Kerja Raya\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) ACT 1984\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS)\n\n(KL-KUALA-SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY) ORDER 2014\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 2 of the Federal Roads\n\n(Private Management) Act 1984 [Act 306], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) This order may be cited as the Federal Roads (Private Management)\n\n(Collection of Tolls) (KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway) Order 2014.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 1 January 2015.\n\nAuthorization to collect tolls\n\n2. (1) The KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway Berhad is authorized for the period\n\nfrom 1 January 2015 to 28 October 2048 to demand, collect and retain the appropriate\n\ntolls specified in column (2) of the First Schedule for the use in either direction of any\n\npart of the road known as the KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway commences from\n\nkilometre 0.00 at coordinates N 366573.829, E 375376.712 Rectified Skew\n\nOrthomorphic (RSO) Geocentric (GDM2000) Grid ending at kilometre 30.70 KL-Kuala\n\nSelangor Expressway at coordinates N 364885.563, E 401792.132 RSO Geocentric\n\n(GDM2000) Grid including Ijok Interchange, Ijok Toll plaza, Puncak Alam Interchange,\n\nKuang Barat Toll Plaza, Kundang Timur Toll Plaza, Kundang Interchange, Kundang\n\nBarat Toll Plaza, Kuang Timur Toll Plaza, Kuang Interchange, Taman Rimba Templer\n\nToll Plaza, Taman Rimba Templer Interchange and its link roads, being a distance of\n\n30.70 kilometres by the classes of vehicle specified in column (1) of the First Schedule.\n\n(2) The roads specified in subparagraph (1) for the use of which tolls are\n\nauthorized to be demanded, collected and retained are shown on the map in the Second\n\nSchedule.\n\nPayment of toll\n\n3. (1) The toll referred to in subparagraph 2(1) shall be payable by the driver of\n\na vehicle before entering the Ijok Toll Plaza situated at kilometre 3.72 at coordinates\n\nN 364234.489, E 377608.060 RSO Geocentric (GDM2000) Grid, Kuang Barat Toll Plaza\n\nsituated at kilometre 13.50 at coordinates N 362137.799, E 386866.042 RSO Geocentric\n\n(GDM2000) Grid, Kundang Timur Toll Plaza situated at kilometre 17.05 at coordinates\n\nN 362088.978, E 390446.108 RSO Geocentric (GDM2000) Grid, Kundang Barat Toll\n\nPlaza situated at kilometre 18.25 at coordinates N 361892.743, E 391573.598 RSO\n\nGeocentric (GDM2000) Grid, Kuang Timur Toll Plaza situated at kilometre 19.60 at\n\ncoordinates N 361957.886, E 392924.944 RSO Geocentric (GDM2000) Grid and Taman\n\nRimba Templer Toll Plaza situated at kilometre 26.75 at coordinates N 363934.443,\n\nE 398646.808 RSO Geocentric (GDM2000) Grid of KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway,\n\nall distance measured from kilometre 0.00 of KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway.\n\n(2) A driver of a vehicle who uses an electronic card or device shall pass\n\nthrough a toll lane having an electronic card or device reader, approach the reader and\n\ntouch the electronic card or device on the reader and the toll payable shall be deducted\n\nfrom the electronic card or device.\n\n(3) A driver of a vehicle who uses an electronic tag shall, before passing\n\nthrough the dedicated electronic tag lane, display the electronic tag or the electronic tag\n\nwith electronic card or device at the windscreen of the vehicle and the toll payable shall\n\nbe deducted from the electronic tag or the electronic tag with electronic card or device.\n\n(4) \"Electronic card or device\" and \"electronic tag\" referred to this paragraph\n\nmeans—\n\n(a) an electronic card or device and electronic tag as approved by the\n\nMinister, issued for the purpose of payment of tolls;\n\n(b) in relation to an electronic card or device, an electronic card or\n\ndevice which is capable of being read by the reader installed at the\n\ntoll lane; and\n\n(c) in relation to an electronic tag, an electronic tag which is capable\n\nof causing the pole at the dedicated electronic tag lane to be raised\n\nelectronically.\n\nExemption from payment of toll\n\n4. Notwithstanding the provisions of this Order, the vehicles specified in the Third\n\nSchedule are exempted from payment of toll.\n\nRevocation\n\n5. The Federal Roads (Private Management) (Collection of Tolls)\n\n(KL-Kuala Selangor Expressway) Order 2011 [P.U. (A) 263/2011] is revoked.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n\n[Subparagraph 2(1)]\n\nPART I\n\nRATES OF TOLLS FOR IJOK TOLL PLAZA, KUANG BARAT TOLL PLAZA, KUANG TIMUR\n\nTOLL PLAZA AND TAMAN RIMBA TEMPLER TOLL PLAZA\n\nFROM 1 JANUARY 2015 TO 28 OCTOBER 2048\n\n( 1 )\n\nClasses of Vehicles\n\n( 2 )\n\nToll Payable\n\nRM\n\n1. Vehicles having two axles and three or four wheels\n\n(excluding taxis and buses)\n\n2.00\n\n2. Vehicles having two axles and five or six wheels\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n4.00\n\n3. Vehicles having three axles or more\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n6.00\n\n4. Taxis 1.00\n\n5. Buses 2.00\n\nFor the purpose of calculating the number of axles and wheels of a vehicle, the axles and\n\nwheels of any trailer towed by the vehicle shall be included as part of the axles and\n\nwheels of the vehicle.\n\nPART II\n\nRATES OF TOLLS FOR KUNDANG TIMUR TOLL PLAZA AND KUNDANG BARAT\n\nTOLL PLAZA\n\nFROM 1 JANUARY 2015 TO 28 OCTOBER 2048\n\n( 1 )\n\nClasses of Vehicles\n\n( 2 )\n\nToll Payable\n\nRM\n\n1. Vehicles having two axles and three or four wheels\n\n(excluding taxis and buses)\n\n1.30\n\n2. Vehicles having two axles and five or six wheels\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n2.60\n\n3. Vehicles having three axles or more\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n3.90\n\n4. Taxis 0.70\n\n5. Buses 1.30\n\nFor the purpose of calculating the number of axles and wheels of a vehicle, the axles and\n\nwheels of any trailer towed by the vehicle shall be included as part of the axles and\n\nwheels of the vehicle.\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n\n[Subparagraph 2(2)]\n\nMAP OF KL-KUALA SELANGOR EXPRESSWAY\n\nTHIRD SCHEDULE\n\n[Paragraph 4]\n\nEXEMPTED VEHICLES\n\n1. Any vehicles carrying the Yang di-Pertuan Agong or the Raja Permaisuri Agong,\n\nthe Rulers or their consorts, the Yang di-Pertua Negeri of the States of Malacca,\n\nPenang, Sabah and Sarawak or their wives, the Dato'-Dato' Undang Negeri\n\nSembilan or the Tengku Besar Tampin or their wives, the Tengku Mahkota or the\n\nRaja Muda of any States or their wives, the Raja Di-Hilir of Perak or his wife,\n\nor any visiting foreign dignitary.\n\n2. Any Government vehicle carrying the Prime Minister or the Deputy Prime\n\nMinister.\n\n3. All military vehicles belonging to the Government or to any visiting force as\n\ndefined in the Visiting Forces Act 1960 [Act 432].\n\n4. All Government vehicles solely engaged in ambulance duties, firefighting duties,\n\npolice duties or rescue duties inclusive of rescue team vehicles from the Civil\n\nDefence Department and vehicles from the Prison Department whilst on\n\nprisoner's escort duties.\n\n5. All vehicles not being Government vehicles solely engaged in ambulance duties,\n\nfirefighting duties and rescue duties.\n\n6. All three-wheeled or four-wheeled motorcycles used by any handicapped person.\n\n7. Vehicles having two axles and two wheels.\n\nMade 17 December 2014\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/28; PN(PU2)426/LVI]\n\nDATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\nMinister of Works"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4745"] = {"id":"MY-H4745","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2016&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":41,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2016年小贩执照（纳闽联邦直辖区）附例","en":"LICENSING OF HAWKERS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2016","orig":"LICENSING OF HAWKERS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2016","ms":"Undang-Undang Kecil Pelesenan Penjaja (Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) 2016","vi":"Quy chế về Cấp phép người bán hàng rong (Lãnh thổ Liên bang Labuan) năm 2016","th":"ข้อบัญญัติการออกใบอนุญาตแผงลอย (เขตการปกครองสหพันธ์ลาบวน) ค.ศ. 2016","id":"Peraturan Daerah Perizinan Pedagang Kaki Lima (Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) Tahun 2016"},"level":"law","category":"03_涉外投资与贸易","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2016","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 41 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\03_涉外投资与贸易\\2016_P.U.(A)344-2016_LICENSING OF HAWKERS (FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2016.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4745-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1.  Nama dan permulaan kuat kuasa"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2.  Tafsiran\n\nBAHAGIAN II\nPELESENAN"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3.  Lesen diperlukan bagi aktiviti penjajaan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4.  Permohonan untuk lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5.  Ketidaklayakan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"ms":"6.  Bentuk lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"text":{"ms":"7.  Fi lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"text":{"ms":"8.  Deposit"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"text":{"ms":"9.  Lesen gantian"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"text":{"ms":"10.  Pindah milik lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"text":{"ms":"11.  Pembaharuan lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"text":{"ms":"12.  Pembatalan lesen\n\nBAHAGIAN III\nPERUNTUKAN AM"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"text":{"ms":"13.  Kandungan lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"text":{"ms":"14.  Larangan\n\nUndang-\nundang\nkecil"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15"},"text":{"ms":"15.  Pemeriksaan perubatan dan kursus asas penyediaan makanan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"text":{"ms":"16.  Kewajipan pemegang lesen"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17"},"text":{"ms":"17.  Pelantikan penama"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18"},"text":{"ms":"18.  Pengambilan pembantu"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19"},"text":{"ms":"19.  Lesen hendaklah berkenaan dengan tapak menjaja tertentu"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20"},"text":{"ms":"20.  Saiz bagi gerai, petak peraga dinding dan kereta tolak"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21"},"text":{"ms":"21.  Pembinaan kajang atau atap di atas petak"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22"},"text":{"ms":"22.  Perobohan dan penyitaan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23"},"text":{"ms":"23.  Larangan bagi aktiviti penjajaan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24"},"text":{"ms":"24.  Penempatan dan pengalihan gerai"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25"},"text":{"ms":"25.  Kenderaan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26"},"text":{"ms":"26.  Penjaja bergerak"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27"},"text":{"ms":"27.  Orang yang dilarang menyediakan makanan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28"},"text":{"ms":"28.  Cara mengendalikan makanan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29"},"text":{"ms":"29.  Tempat di mana penyediaan makanan dilarang"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30"},"text":{"ms":"30.  Kehendak kebersihan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31"},"text":{"ms":"31.  Larangan penjualan makanan tidak selamat"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32"},"text":{"ms":"32.  Petak menjaja tidak boleh diserah hak, dipajak, disewa atau disewa kecil"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33"},"text":{"ms":"33.  Perubahan barang yang telah dilesenkan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A34","no":34,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 34"},"text":{"ms":"34.  Waktu menjalankan aktiviti penjajaan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35"},"text":{"ms":"35.  Bekalan air"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36"},"text":{"ms":"36.  Perobohan, penyitaan dan tuntutan"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37"},"text":{"ms":"37.  Kacau ganggu"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38"},"text":{"ms":"38.  Kuasa untuk menghendaki maklumat"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A39","no":39,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 39"},"text":{"ms":"39.  Pengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A40","no":40,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 40"},"text":{"ms":"40.  Penalti"}},{"id":"MY-H4745-A41","no":41,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 41"},"text":{"ms":"41.  Pembatalan dan peruntukan peralihan\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\nJADUAL KEDUA\nJADUAL KETIGA\n\nAKTA KERAJAAN TEMPATAN 1976\n\nUNDANG-UNDANG KECIL PELESENAN PENJAJA\n(WILAYAH PERSEKUTUAN LABUAN) 2016\n\nPADA menjalankan kuasa yang diberikan oleh perenggan 73(1)(g)\nAkta Kerajaan Tempatan 1976 [ Akta 171] (sebagaimana yang diperluas dan diubahsuai\noleh Peri ntah Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan (Pemerluasan dan Ubah Suaian Akta\nKerajaan Tempatan 1976) 2010 [ P.U. (A) 439 /2010]), Perbadanan Labuan membuat,\ndan m enurut seksyen 103 Akta,  Menteri mengesahkan , undang-undang kecil\nyang berikut:\n\nBAHAGIAN I\nPERMULAAN\n\nNama dan permulaan kuat kuasa\n1. (1) Undang-undang kecil ini bolehlah dinamakan Undang-Undang Kecil\nPelesenan Penjaja (Wilayah Persekutuan Labuan) 2016.\n\n(2) Undang-Undang Kecil ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 Januari 2017.\n\nTafsiran\n2. Dalam Undang-Undang Kecil ini, melainkan jika konteksnya menghendaki makna\nyang lain—\n\n\"aktiviti penjajaan\" ertinya menjual atau menawarkan untuk jualan apa -apa\nbarang di sesuatu tapak menjaja;\n\n\"barang\" termasuklah apa -apa jenis makanan, perkhidmatan yang di beri atau\napa-apa jenis barang yang lain;\n\n\"fi lesen\" ertinya kadar bayaran yang ditetapkan bagi sesuatu lesen yang\ndikeluarkan di bawah Undang -Undang Kecil ini sebagaimana yang dinyatakan dalam\nJadual Pertama;\n\n\"gerai\" ertinya struktur yang didirikan untu k tujuan menjaja yang di atasnya\natau di dalamnya barang-barang dijual atau dipamerkan untuk jualan di tapak menjaja;\n\n\"kenderaan\" ertinya suatu van, kereta tolak atau apa -apa kenderaan lain yang\ndiluluskan oleh Perbadanan untuk digunakan bagi tujuan menjaja;\n\n\"makanan\" termasuklah tiap -tiap barang yang dikilangkan, dijual atau\ndigambarkan untuk digunakan sebagai makanan atau minuman bagi kegunaan manusia\natau yang diguna di dalam ko mposisi, penyediaan  dan pengawetan mana-mana\nmakanan atau minuman bagi kegu naan manusia dan termasuklah konfeksi, bahan\nkunyahan dan apa -apa bahan lain untuk makanan, minuman, konfeksi atau bahan\nkunyahan itu;\n\n\"pemegang lesen\" ertinya mana -mana orang yang kepadanya lesen penjaja\ndikeluarkan di bawah Undang-Undang Kecil ini;\n\n\"penjaja\" ertinya seseorang penjaja bergerak, penjaja sementara atau penjaja\nstatik yang dilesenkan di bawah Undang-Undang Kecil ini;\n\n\"penjaja bergerak\" ertinya mana-mana orang yang dengan atau tanpa kenderaan\npergi dari setempat ke setempat di mana -mana jal an untuk menjual atau\nmempamerkan untuk jualan apa-apa barang;\n\n\"penjaja sementara\" ertinya mana -mana orang yang menjual atau\nmempamerkan untuk jualan apa -apa barang di gerai atau petak yang ditetapkan di\nmana-mana jalan bagi maksud itu oleh Perbadanan untuk apa -apa tempoh dan\nmengikut waktu perniagaan yang ditetapkan oleh Perbadanan;\n\n\"penjaja statik\" ertinya mana -mana orang yang menjual atau mempamerkan\nuntuk jualan apa-apa barang di gerai atau petak di mana -mana jalan atau di mana-mana\npetak peraga dinding;\n\n\"penyediaan makanan\" atau \"menyediakan makanan\" termasuklah\nmengendalikan, menghidang atau menjual makanan;\n\n\"Perbadanan\" ertinya Perbadanan Labuan yang ditubuhkan di bawah seksyen 3\nAkta Perbadanan Labuan 2001 [Akta 609];\n\n\"perkakas\" termasuklah bekas, alat-alat, kerusi, meja, kelengkapan atau apa -apa\nbenda lain yang digunakan berkaitan dengan aktiviti penjajaan;\n\n\"petak\" ertinya mana -mana ruang yang ditandakan oleh Perbadanan di tapak\nmenjaja bagi menjalankan aktiviti penjajaan;\n\n\"petak peraga dinding\" ertinya suat u struktur yang diluluskan oleh  Perbadanan\nyang dibina di atas atau bersebelahan mana -mana bahagian luar dinding sesebuah\nbangunan;\n\n\"tapak menjaja\" ertinya mana -mana bangunan, jalan atau kawasan  di mana\naktiviti penjajaan dibenarkan oleh Perbadanan pada hari atau waktu yang ditentukan\noleh Perbadanan.\n\nBAHAGIAN II\nPELESENAN\n\nLesen diperlukan bagi aktiviti penjajaan\n3. (1) Mana-mana orang boleh menjalankan aktiviti sebagai seorang penjaja\napabila suatu lesen penjaja dikeluarkan oleh Perbadanan di bawah Undang -Undang\nKecil ini.\n\n(2) Mana-mana orang yang melanggar perenggan (1) melakukan suatu\nkesalahan.\n\nPermohonan untuk lesen\n4. (1) Tertakluk kepada undang -undang kecil 3, sesuatu permohonan untuk\nsuatu lesen di bawah Undang -Undang Kecil ini hendaklah dibuat dalam apa -apa bentuk\ndan cara sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Perbadanan.\n\n(2) Perbadanan boleh meluluskan atau tidak meluluskan sesuatu\npermohonan untuk suatu lesen di bawah Undang-Undang Kecil ini.\n\n(3) Perbadanan boleh, jika difikirk an perlu, menghendaki mana -mana\npemohon untuk hadir sendiri bagi memberi apa -apa dokumen atau maklumat lanjut\nberkaitan dengan sesuatu permohonan untuk suatu lesen.\n\n(4) Suatu lesen yang dikeluarkan di bawah Undang -Undang Kecil ini adalah\ntertakluk kepada—\n\n(a) tempoh lesen sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Perbadanan;\n\n(b) perjanjian penyewaan tapak menjaja ditandatangani oleh\npemohon, jika Perbadanan fikirkan perlu;\n\n(c) peruntukan Undang -Undang Kecil ini, syarat -syarat dan\nsekatan-sekatan yang dikenakan  oleh Perbadanan dan oleh\nmana-mana pihak berkuasa yang berkenaan;\n\n(d) bayaran deposit sebagaimana yang diperuntukkan dalam\nundang-undang kecil 8;\n\n(e) bayaran fi lesen sebagaima na yang ditetapkan dalam Jadual\nPertama; dan\n\n(f) apa-apa kehendak yang lain di bawah mana -mana undang-undang\nyang berkaitan.\n\n(5)      Perbadanan boleh, dari semasa ke semasa dan semasa sesuatu lesen masih\nberkuat kuasa, mengenakan apa -apa syarat tambahan ke atas lesen itu atau mengubah\natau membatalkan apa-apa syarat yang dikenakan ke atas lesen itu.\n\n(6)  Suatu notis bertulis hendaklah diberikan kepada pemegang lesen sebelum\nPerbadanan membuat apa-apa keputusan di bawah perenggan (5).\n\nKetidaklayakan\n5. Walau apa pun  undang-undang kecil 4, tiada lesen boleh dikeluarkan di bawah\nUndang-Undang Kecil ini kepada mana-mana orang yang—\n\n(a) bukan warganegara Malaysia; atau\n\n(b) berumur di bawah lapan belas tahun.\n\nBentuk lesen\n6. Suatu lesen yang dikeluarkan di bawah Undang -Undang Kecil ini he ndaklah\ndalam apa-apa bentuk sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Perbadanan.\n\nFi lesen\n7. (1) Fi lesen  yang k ena dibayar bagi pengeluaran s uatu lesen di bawah\nUndang-Undang Kecil ini adalah sebagaimana yang dinyatakan dalam Jadual Pertama.\n\n(2) Perbadanan boleh mengecualikan mana -mana pemegang lesen daripada\ntanggungan untuk membayar kesemua atau mana-mana bahagian daripada fi lesen.\n\n(3) Fi lesen yang dibayar di bawah perenggan (1) tidak boleh dibayar balik.\n\nDeposit\n8. (1) Perbadanan boleh menghendaki mana -mana orang yang kepadanya lesen\ntelah dikeluarkan untuk membayar deposit sejumlah wang yang tidak melebihi lima\npuluh ribu ringgit untuk memastikan bahawa peruntuk an Akta, Undang -Undang Kecil,\nsyarat atau sekatan lesen dipatuhi.\n\n(2) Walau apa pun perenggan (1), Perbadanan boleh, jika difikirkan perlu,\nmengecualikan mana -mana pemegang lesen daripada tanggungan untuk membayar\nkeseluruhan atau sebahagian deposit.\n\n(3) Sekiranya terdapat pelanggaran mana -mana peruntuka n Akta,\nUndang-Undang Kecil, syarat atau sekatan lesen, Perbadanan hendaklah memberi notis\nkepada pemegang lesen dalam tempoh yang ditetapkan dalam notis untuk memberi\nrepresentasi kenapa depositnya tidak boleh dilucuthakkan.\n\n(4) Perbadanan boleh, setelah mempertimbangkan repres entasi yang\ndikemukakan oleh pemegang lesen atau jika pemegang lesen gagal membuat\nrepresentasi, memutuskan sama ada untuk melucuthakkan keseluruhan atau\nsebahagian deposit.\n\n(5) Tertakluk kepada perenggan (4), Perbadanan boleh menghendaki\npemegang lesen u ntuk menggantikan keseluruhan atau sebahagian deposit yang telah\ndilucuthakkan.\n\n(6) Deposit yang dibayar hendaklah, melainkan dilucuthakkan, dibayar balik\nkepada pemegang lesen tanpa apa -apa pelarasan bagi faedah atas amaun yang\ndiberikan di bawah perengg an (1) selepas pemeg ang lesen berhenti menjalankan\naktiviti penjajaan di tapak menjajanya.\n\n(7) Pemegang lesen hendaklah memaklumkan kepada Perbadanan jika dia\ntelah berhenti menjalankan aktiviti penjajaan di tapak menjajanya.\n\n(8) Walau apa pun  perenggan (7), pemegang lesen hendaklah memohon\nkepada Perbadanan dalam tempoh tiga puluh hari dari tarikh dia berhenti menjalankan\naktiviti penjajaan itu untuk depositnya dibayar balik.\n\n(9) Sekiranya pemegang lesen tidak memohon untuk depositnya dibayar\nbalik ata u depositnya tidak dituntut dalam tempoh yang dinyatakan di bawah\nperenggan (8), deposit tersebut akan dilucuthakkan dan hendaklah dibayar ke dalam\n\nKumpulan Wang Perbadanan Labuan dan hendaklah menjadi sebahagian daripada hasil\nkumpulan wang itu.\n\nLesen gantian\n9. Jika Perbadanan berpuas hati bahawa suatu lesen yang sah yang dikeluarkan\ndi bawah Undang -Undang Kecil ini telah hilang, cacat atau rosak, Perbadanan boleh\nmengeluarkan lesen gantian.\n\nPindah milik lesen\n10. (1) Tiada pemegang lesen boleh  memindah milik lesennya kepada\nmana-mana pihak yang lain.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perenggan (1) melakukan\nsuatu kesalahan.\n\nPembaharuan lesen\n11. (1) Suatu lesen yang dikeluarkan di bawah Undang -Undang Kecil ini tida k\nboleh diperbaharui sebagai suatu hak dan sesuatu permohonan untuk memperbaharui\nsuatu lesen hendaklah dianggap sebagai permohonan untuk suatu lesen.\n\n(2) Sesuatu permohonan untuk memperbaharui suatu lesen hendaklah\ndibuat dalam tempoh enam puluh hari seb elum tarikh tamat lesen itu dan hendaklah\ndibuat dalam apa-apa bentuk dan cara sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Perbadanan.\n\n(3) Perbadanan boleh, jika difikirkan perlu, menghendaki mana -mana\npemohon untuk hadir sendiri bagi memberi apa -apa dokumen atau ma klumat lanjut\nberkaitan dengan sesuatu permohonan untuk memperbaharui suatu lesen.\n\n(4) Perbadanan boleh memperbaharui atau tidak memperbaharui lesen itu\ndan hendaklah memaklumkan pemohon keputusannya itu secara bertulis atau melalui\napa-apa cara lain sebagaimana yang akan ditentukan oleh Perbadanan dan membayar\nbalik deposit kepada pemohon tertakluk kepada undang-undang kecil 8(9).\n\n(5) Suatu lesen jika diperbaharui di bawah perenggan (4 ) adalah tertakluk\nkepada—\n\n(a) tempoh lesen sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Perbadanan;\n\n(b) bayaran fi lesen sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam Jadual\nPertama;\n\n(c) peruntukan Undang -Undang Kecil ini, syarat dan sekatan yang\ndikenakan oleh Perbadanan dan oleh mana -mana pihak berkuasa\nyang berkenaan;\n\n(d) pemegang lesen ti dak mempunyai tunggakan sewa di tapak\nmenjajanya; dan\n\n (e) perjanjian penyewaan masih berkuat kuasa.\n\n(6) Tiada deposit lanjut perlu diberi oleh pemegang lesen jika lesennya\ndiperbaharui.\n\n(7) Perbadanan tidak akan bertanggungjawab untuk membayar apa -apa\npampasan kepada pemegang lesen sekiranya lesen tidak d iperbaharui di bawah\nperenggan (4).\n\nPembatalan lesen\n12. (1) Perbadanan boleh membatalkan suatu lesen yan g dikeluarkan di bawah\nundang-undang kecil 4 jika ia berpuas hati bahawa—\n\n(a) pemegang lesen it u telah melanggar mana -mana peruntukan Akta,\nUndang-Undang Kecil, syarat atau sekatan lesen;\n\n(b) pemegang lesen itu telah, sama ada berkaitan dengan sesuatu\npermohonan untuk suatu lesen itu atau pada bila -bila masa\n\nselepas suatu lesen dikeluarkan, mengemukakan kepada\nPerbadanan suatu dokumen atau perisytiharan yang palsu,\nmengelirukan atau tidak tepat; atau\n\n(c) pemegang lesen itu tidak menjalankan aktiviti penjajaan yang\ndilesenkan selama tempoh tiga bulan berturut -turut tanpa\nmemaklumkan kepada Perbadanan.\n\n(2) Pembatalan lesen di bawah perenggan (1) boleh dibuat oleh Perbadanan\ntanpa apa -apa bayaran pampasan kepada pemegang lesen  dan Perbadanan boleh\nmelucuthakkan keseluruhan deposit yang telah dibayar di bawah undang -undang\nkecil 8.\n\n(3) Sebelum suatu lesen dibatalkan , Perbadanan hendaklah memberi notis\nsecara bertulis kepada pemegang lesen menghendaki dia membuat representasi dalam\ntempoh sebagaimana yang dinyatakan dalam notis kenapa lesennya tidak boleh\ndibatalkan.\n\n(4) Selepas tamat tem poh masa yang dinyatakan di dalam notis di bawah\nperenggan (3) dan setelah menimbangkan representasi pemegang lesen atau jika\npemegang lesen gagal membuat representasi, Perbadanan hendaklah terus\nmempertimbangkan perkara tersebut dan memaklumkan keputusannya dalam notis\nbertulis kepada pemegang lesen.\n\n (5) Jika Perbadanan memutuskan untuk membatalkan lesen itu, pembatalan\nlesen itu hendaklah mula berkuat  kuasa pada tarikh yang dinyatakan dalam notis yang\ndiserahkan kepada pemegang lesen.\n\n(6) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang  menjalankan aktiviti penjajaan setelah\nlesennya dibatalkan di bawah perenggan (5) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nBAHAGIAN III\nPERUNTUKAN AM\n\nKandungan lesen\n13. Suatu lesen yang dikeluarkan oleh Perbadanan kepada seseorang pemegang\nlesen di bawah Undang -Undang Kecil ini hendaklah mengandungi butir -butir yang\nberikut:\n\n(a) nama, alamat terbaharu dan nombor kad pengenalan pemegang lesen;\n\n(b) gambar terbaharu berukuran pasport pemegang lesen;\n\n(c) jenis penjaja;\n\n(d) tempoh sah lesen;\n\n(e) jenis barang yang akan dijual;\n\n(f) nama, alamat terba haru, nombor kad pengenalan  dan gambar terba haru\nberukuran pasport pembantu yang diambil kerja oleh pemegang lesen,\njika ada;\n\n(g) tempoh dan waktu menjaja;\n\n(h) tapak menjaja; dan\n\n(i) apa-apa syarat dan sekatan yang lain yang dikenakan oleh Perbadanan.\n\nLarangan\n14. (1) Tiada pemegang lesen boleh—\n\n(a) mengambil bekerja mana -mana orang di bawah umur lapan belas\ntahun;\n\n(b) mengambil bekerja mana-mana warga asing;\n\n(c) membenarkan apa -apa a ktiviti perjudian atau aktiviti  tidak\nbermoral atau membena rkan apa -apa perbuatan yang boleh\nmenyebabkan kacau ganggu, gangguan, kecederaan atau\nkebisingan kepada penduduk di kawasan persekitaran tapak\nmenjaja; dan\n\n(d) menjalankan aktiviti yang lain di tapak menjaja selain daripada\naktiviti penjajaan yang dinyatakan dalam lesennya.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perenggan (1) melakukan\nsuatu kesalahan.\n\nPemeriksaan perubatan dan kursus asas penyediaan makanan\n15. (1) Mana-mana orang yang terlibat dalam penyediaan makanan untuk aktiviti\npenjajaan hendaklah—\n\n(a) menjalani pemeriksaan perubatan sebagaimana yang Perbadanan\narahkan;\n\n(b) mendapatkan suntikan pelalian terhadap penyakit berjangkit; dan\n\n(c) menghadiri kursus asas penyediaan makanan yang diiktiraf oleh\nKementerian Kesihatan Malaysia.\n\n(2) Pemeriksaan perubatan dan suntikan pelalian terhadap penyakit\nberjangkit hendaklah dijalankan oleh pegawai perubatan atau kesihatan yang berdaftar\ndi bawah Akta Perubatan 1971 [Akta 50].\n\n(3) Pemegang lesen hendaklah—\n\n(a) mematuhi keperluan perenggan (1) sekiranya pemegang lesen itu\nsendiri akan terlibat dalam penyediaan makanan  untuk aktiviti\npenjajaan; dan\n\n(b) memastikan penamanya yang dilantik  di bawah undang -undang\nkecil 17  dan pembantu nya yang diambil bekerja  di bawah\nundang-undang kecil 18  yang terlibat dalam penyediaan makanan\nmematuhi keperluan perenggan (1).\n\n(4) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang tidak mematuhi perenggan (3 )\nmelakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\n(5) Walau apa pun perenggan (1), mana -mana orang yang terlibat dalam\npenyediaan makanan  untuk ak tiviti penjajaan boleh diarahkan oleh Perbadanan pada\nbila-bila masa untuk—\n\n(a) menjalani pemeriksaan perubatan;\n\n(b) mendapatkan suntikan pelalian terhadap penyakit berjangkit; dan\n\n(c) menghadiri kursus asas berkaitan dengan penyediaan makanan.\n\n(6) Mana-mana orang yang tidak mematuhi perenggan (5) melakukan suatu\nkesalahan.\n\nKewajipan pemegang lesen\n16. (1) Seseorang p emegang lesen hendaklah pada setiap masa hadir untuk\nmenjalankan atau mengawasi aktiviti penjajaannya.\n\n(2) Walau apa pun perenggan (1) , jika pemegang lesen tidak dapat hadir\nuntuk menjalankan aktiviti penjajaannya selama tempoh tiga puluh hari atau lebih, dia\nhendaklah—\n\n(a) melantik seorang penama di bawah undan g-undang kecil 17  bagi\nmenggantikannya; atau\n\n(b) menutup sementara petak yang diperuntukkan kepadanya.\n\n(3) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perenggan (1) dan (2)\nmelakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nPelantikan penama\n17. (1) Sesuatu permohonan untuk seorang penama di bawah undang-undang\nkecil 16(2)(a) hendaklah dibuat dalam apa -apa bentuk dan cara  yang ditentukan oleh\nPerbadanan.\n\n(2) Perbadanan boleh—\n\n(a) menghendaki pemegang lesen untuk mengemukakan maklumat\nlanjut bagi maksud mempertimbangkan permohonan tersebut;\natau\n\n(b) meluluskan permohonan itu tertakluk kepada syarat yang lain atau\nmenolak permohonan itu.\n\n(3) Fi yang kena dibayar oleh pemegang lesen bagi permohonan pelantikan\nseorang penama hendaklah sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam Jadual Kedua.\n\n(4) Seseorang penama yang dilantik di bawah perenggan (2) hendaklah\ntertakluk kepada Undang -Undang Kecil ini, syarat dan sekatan yang dikenakan oleh\nPerbadanan ke atas pemegang lesen dan mempunyai tanggungan yang sama\nsebagaimana seorang pemegang lesen.\n\nPengambilan pembantu\n18. (1) Seseorang p emegang lesen tidak boleh mengambil bekerja mana-mana\norang sebagai pembantu tanpa kelulusan bertulis daripada Perbadanan terlebih dahulu.\n\n(2) Sesuatu permohonan bagi suatu kelulusan di bawah perenggan (1)\nhendaklah dibuat dalam apa -apa bentuk dan cara sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh\nPerbadanan.\n\n(3) Perbadanan boleh—\n\n(a) menghendaki pemegang lesen untuk mengemukakan maklumat\nlanjut bagi maksud mempertimbangkan permohonan tersebut;\natau\n\n(b) meluluskan permohonan itu tertakluk kepada syarat yang lain atau\nmenolak permohonan itu.\n\n(4) Pengambilan kerja seseorang pembantu tidak mengecualikan pemegang\nlesen daripada undang-undang kecil 16(1).\n\n(5) Mana-mana p embantu yang diambil bekerja di bawah perenggan (4)\nadalah tertakluk kepada—\n\n(a) peruntukan Undang -Undang Kecil, syarat dan sekatan yang\ndikenakan oleh Perbadanan di bawah  undang-undang kecil 4(4);\ndan\n\n(b) apa-apa syarat yang lain yang ditetapkan oleh Perbadanan\ndi bawah subperenggan 3(b).\n\n(6) Walau apa pun  undang-undang kecil ini, m ana-mana pemegang lesen\nyang melanggar perenggan (1) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nLesen hendaklah berkenaan dengan tapak menjaja tertentu\n19. (1) Lesen yang  dikeluarkan di bawah  undang-undang kecil 4 hendaklah\nberkenaan dengan sesuatu tapak menjaja tertentu sebagaimana yang dinyatakan dalam\nlesen itu.\n\n(2) Walau apa pun perenggan (1), Perbadanan boleh, menurut budi bicaranya\natas suatu permohonan yang dibuat oleh seorang pemegang lesen, membenarkan\npemindahan tapak menjaja ke suatu tapak menjaja yang lain untuk menjual barang yang\nsama tertakluk kepada—\n\n(a) pembayaran fi sebagaimana yang ditetapkan dalam Jadual Kedua;\n\n(b) pemegang lesen tidak mempunyai tunggakan sewa di tapak\nmenjaja asal;\n\n(c) pemegang lesen menandatangani perjanjian penyewaan untuk\npenggunaan tapak menjaja yang lain, jika Perbadanan fikirkan\nperlu; dan\n\n(d) arahan yang lain sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Perbadanan.\n\n(3) Perbadanan boleh, jika difikirkan perlu  dan sesuai, memberi notis secara\nbertulis kepada pemegang lesen untuk memindahkan tapak menjaja yang telah\ndiperuntukkan kepadanya kepad a suatu tapak menjaja yang lain dalam tempoh yang\nditetapkan oleh Perbadanan dalam notis itu.\n\n(4) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang tidak mematuhi notis di bawah\nperenggan (3) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\n(5) Pemegang lesen yang  tapak menjajanya dipindahkan di bawah\nperenggan (3) tidak berhak untuk menuntut apa-apa pampasan daripada Perbadanan.\n\nSaiz bagi gerai, petak peraga dinding dan kereta tolak\n20. (1) Saiz maksimum bagi gerai ialah 5 meter panjang dan 3 meter lebar\nmelainkan gerai yang dibina oleh Perbadanan.\n\n(2) Tiada petak peraga dinding boleh melebihi 4 meter panjang kali 2 meter\ntinggi kali 1 meter lebar.\n\n(3) Kereta tolak yang digunakan oleh penjaja bergerak tidak boleh melebihi 2\nmeter panjang dan 1 meter lebar dan atap atau kajang d i atasnya tidak boleh\ndilanjutkan lebih daripada 1 meter daripada mana-mana bahagian kereta tolak itu.\n\n(4) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar undang -undang kecil ini\nmelakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nPembinaan kajang atau atap di atas petak\n21. (1) Tiada k ajang atau apa -apa jenis atap atau struktur boleh dibina\ndi mana-mana tapak menjaja, melainkan dibenarkan oleh Perbadanan, tertakluk kepada\napa-apa syarat yang Perbadanan fikirkan perlu.\n\n(2) Pembinaan sesuatu kajang atau atap atau struktu r yang dibenarkan\ndi bawah perenggan (1) hendaklah mengikut syarat-syarat yang dikenakan oleh\nPerbadanan.\n\n(3) Kebenaran yang diberi di bawah perenggan (1) boleh ditarik balik pada\nbila-bila masa oleh Perbadanan apabila dib eritahu secara bertulis ketidakpatuhan\nmana-mana syarat yang ditetapkan di bawah perenggan (1) dan pemegang lesen\n\nhendaklah merobohkan kajang, atap atau struktur itu dalam tempoh yang ditetapkan\noleh Perbadanan dalam notis itu.\n\n(4) Jika pemegang lesen gagal mematuhi not is di bawah perenggan (3),\nPerbadanan boleh meroboh kan kajang atau atap atau struktur itu dan Perbadanan\nboleh mendapat kan kembali perbelanjaan yang ditanggung oleh Perbadanan untuk\nkerja perobohan itu daripada pemegang lesen.\n\n(5) Perbadanan tidak akan be rtanggungjawab untuk membayar apa -apa\npampasan kepada pemegang lesen untuk tindakan yang telah dia mbil di bawah\nundang-undang kecil ini.\n\n(6) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perenggan (1) atau (2)\nmelakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nPerobohan dan penyitaan\n22. (1) Perbadanan boleh memberi notis secara bertulis kepada  pemegang lesen\nuntuk merobohkan mana-mana gerai, petak peraga dinding, kajang, atap atau struktur\ndi atas mana-mana gerai atau petak yang didirikan—\n\n(a) yang tidak mengikut ukuran yan g diteta pkan di bawah\nundang-undang kecil 20; atau\n\n(b) tanpa kebenaran Perbadanan,\n\ndalam tempoh yang ditetapkan oleh Perbadanan dalam notis itu.\n\n(2) Jika pemegang lesen gagal mem atuhi notis di bawah perenggan (1),\nPerbadanan, selepas tamat tempoh ya ng dinyatakan dalam notis itu , boleh mengambil\nlangkah u ntuk merobohkan gerai, petak peraga dinding, kaj ang, atap atau struktur\ndi atas  petak itu tanpa membayar apa-apa pampasan kepada pemegang lesen dan\nPerbadanan boleh menuntut kos perobohan daripada pemegang lesen  itu.\n\n(3) Perbadanan boleh menyita mana-mana kenderaan yang digunakan untuk\naktiviti penjajaan tanpa kelulusan Perbadanan atau kereta tolak yang digunakan oleh\nmana-mana pemegang lesen yang tidak mengikut  ukuran yang ditetapkan untuk kereta\ntolak yang digunakan untuk aktiviti penjajaan di bawah undang-undang kecil 20(3).\n\n(4) Mana-mana pemegang lesen boleh menuntut kenderaan atau kereta tolak\nyang telah disita di  bawah perenggan (3) da lam tempoh yang ditentukan oleh\nPerbadanan tertakluk kepada undang-undang kecil 36(3).\n\n(5) Perbadanan tidak akan bertanggungjawab ke atas sebarang kerosakan\ndan kerugian yang ditanggung oleh pemegang lesen akibat daripada tindakan yang\ndiambil oleh Perbadanan di bawah undang-undang kecil ini.\n\nLarangan bagi aktiviti penjajaan\n23. (1) Tiada pemegang lesen boleh menjalankan aktiviti penjajaannya—\n\n(a) dalam lingkungan 9 meter daripada simpang jalan; atau\n\n(b) dalam lingkungan 3.6 meter daripada pili bomba.\n\n(2) Tiada pemegang lesen boleh menjalankan aktiviti penjajaannya den gan\ncara yang boleh menghalang atau mengganggu kelancaran arus lalu  lintas kenderaan\ndan pergerakan bebas pejalan kaki.\n\n(3) Tiada pemegang lesen atau pembantunya boleh menggunakan pelaung,\npembesar suara, mikrofon atau apa -apa alat yang lain untuk mempert ingkatkan bunyi\nsemasa menjalankan aktiviti penjajanya.\n\n(4) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar undang -undang kecil ini\nmelakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nPenempatan dan pengalihan gerai\n24. (1) Seseorang p emegang lesen hendaklah mematuhi apa -apa arahan li san\natau bertulis yang diberi oleh Perbadanan dari semasa ke semasa berkenaan  dengan\npenempatan gerai, b arang atau lain -lain perkakas yang berkaitan dengan aktiviti\npenjajaannya di mana-mana tapak menjaja.\n\n(2) Seseorang penjaja sementara hendaklah mengali hkan gerainya,\nkenderaan, barang dan lain-lain perkakas yang berkaitan dengan aktiviti penjajaannya\napabila tempoh dan waktu penjajaan tamat.\n\n(3) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perenggan (1) atau (2)\nmelakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nKenderaan\n25. (1) Seseorang p emegang lesen yang menggunakan kenderaan bagi maksud\nmenjalankan aktiviti penjajaan  hendaklah memastikan kenderaan itu mengikut ukuran\natau bentuk sebagaimana yang ditentukan oleh Perbadanan.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perengga n (1) melakukan\nsuatu kesalahan.\n\nPenjaja bergerak\n26. (1) Seseorang penjaja bergerak melainkan penjaja bergerak yang\nmenggunakan van hendaklah sentiasa bergerak kecuali pada waktu menjual barang\nkepada pelanggan.\n\n(2) Penjaja bergerak yang menggunakan van  hendaklah menjalankan aktiviti\npenjajaan di petak yang dibenarkan oleh Perbadanan dalam tempoh dan waktu yang\nditentukan dalam lesen dan hendaklah memindahkan vannya daripada petak itu apabila\ntempoh dan waktu penjajaan tamat.\n\n(3) Tiada penjaja bergerak yang menggunakan van boleh meletakkan atau\nmempamerkan untuk jualan barang yang digunakan atau berhubung dengan aktiviti\npenjajaannya di luar van.\n\n(4) Mana-mana penjaja bergerak yang melanggar undang -undang kecil ini\nmelakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nOrang yang dilarang menyediakan makanan\n27. (1) Mana-mana orang yang menghidap atau membawa apa -apa penyakit\nyang berjangkit tidak boleh terlibat dalam penyediaan makanan  untuk aktiviti\npenjajaan.\n\n(2) Mana-mana orang yang melanggar perenggan (1) melakukan suatu\nkesalahan.\n\nCara mengendalikan makanan\n28. (1) Mana-mana pemegang lesen atau  pembantunya yang terlibat dalam\npenyediaan makanan—\n\n(a) hendaklah memastikan makanan yang ditawarkan untuk jualan\nadalah bersih dan selamat untuk dimakan dan diminum;\n\n(b) hendaklah menggunakan sepit, penyeduk, sarung tangan plastik\natau lain-lain perkakas yang sesuai bagi penyediaan makanan;\n\n(c) tidak boleh mengguna kan jari-jarinya untuk menyentuh\nmana-mana bahagian anggota badan nya yang lain  semasa\npenyediaan makanan;\n\n(d) tidak boleh mengguna kan nafasnya untuk membuka mana -mana\nbeg atau pembalut untuk jualan makanan;\n\n(e) tidak boleh menyapu tangannya dengan bajunya atau dengan\napa-apa cara selain dari pada menggunakan tuala atau kain yang\nbersih;\n\n(f) tidak bo leh batuk atau bersin berhampiran dengan mana -mana\nmakanan;\n\n(g) tidak boleh merokok;\n\n(h) hendaklah menjaga diri dan pakaiannya supaya berada dalam\nkeadaan bersih dan hendaklah pada setiap masa memakai apron,\npenutup kepala dan apa -apa benda lain sebagaimana yang\ndiarahkan oleh Perbadanan dari semasa ke semasa;\n\n(i) tidak boleh mempunyai luka atau pecah kulit pada tangan atau\njarinya; dan\n\n(j) hendaklah menggunakan tuala bersih untuk tujuan mengelap atau\nmembersih apa -apa bungkusan atau alat yang digunaka n untuk\npenyediaan makanan.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen atau  pembantunya yang melanggar\nperenggan (1) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nTempat di mana penyediaan makanan dilarang\n29. (1) Seseorang pe megang lesen atau pembantunya tidak boleh menyediakan\nmakanan—\n\n(a) dalam mana-mana tandas atau bilik air;\n\n(b)  di mana -mana tempat di mana apa -apa benda atau binatang\ndibiarkan berada atau disimpan; atau\n\n(c) di mana-mana tempat di mana makanan itu berkemungkinan akan\ntercemar atau menjadi kurang baik atau kebersihan makanan akan\nterjejas.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen atau pembantunya yang melanggar\nperenggan (1) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nKehendak kebersihan\n30. (1) Seseorang pemegang lesen dan pembantunya hendaklah memastikan—\n\n(a) apa-apa jenis makanan untuk jualan  dijual dan  disediakan di atas\npermukaan yang ketinggiannya 0.5 meter dari pada permukaan\ntanah atau lantai;\n\n(b) tapak menjaja diselenggara supaya berada dalam keadaan bersih\npada setiap masa;\n\n(c) kawasan di sekitar yang hampir sekali di hadapan, di belakang dan\ndi tepi tapak menjaja yang diperuntukkan kepada  pemegang lesen\nberada dalam keadaan bersih;\n\n(d) makanan yang ditawarkan untuk jualan hendaklah berada dalam\nkeadaan bersih dan ditutup dengan penutup makanan pada setiap\nmasa;\n\n(e) kenderaan yang digunakan untuk menjaja atau mengangkut\nmakanan untuk jualan sentiasa berada dalam keadaan bersih;\n\n(f) perkakas dan lekapan yang digunakan dalam aktiviti penjajaannya\nhendaklah berada dalam keadaan bersih;\n\n(g) hanya bekas atau alat pembungkusan yang ditentukan atau\ndibenarkan oleh Perbadanan digunakan untuk membungkus\nmakanan untuk jualan;\n\n(h) makanan untuk pelanggan tidak dibungkus dengan kertas yang\ntidak bersih atau kertas yang terdapat bahan tulisan atau cetakan\ndi atasnya atau dengan bahan yang boleh mencemarkan m akanan\nitu;\n\n(i) segala perkakas  yang digunakan dalam aktiviti penjajaannya\ndisimpan di tempat yang sesuai dan berada dalam keadaan bersih;\n\n(j) pemegang lesen dan pembantunya sentiasa berpakaian bersih dan\nhendaklah memakai apron dan penutup kepala;\n\n(k) tong sampah daripada apa -apa jenis dan uku ran sebagaimana\nditentukan oleh  Perbadanan disediakan dengan secukupnya;\n\n(l) semua sampah dikumpul dan dibungkus dalam beg plastik dan\ndimasukkan ke dalam bekas bertutup yang disediakan bagi\nmaksud itu, dan hend aklah memastikan semua bekas itu\ndikosongkan dan dibersihkan seberapa kerap yang perlu untuk\nmenjaga kebersihan pada setiap masa;\n\n(m) kertas atau bahan yang tidak bersih tidak boleh digunakan untuk\nmembungkus barang-barang;\n\n(n) bungkusan atau bekas yang digunakan untuk membungkus buah\ndan sayur tidak boleh dibuat daripada bahan yang akan\nmencemarkan atau menukar warna atau rasa buah atau sayur itu,\natau menyebabkan buah atau sayur itu dalam keadaan yang\nmemudaratkan kesihatan; dan\n\n(o) apa-apa racun atau apa-apa bahan yang berbahaya atau apa -apa\nbahan lain yang mungkin mencemar keadaan baik barang untuk\njualan tidak boleh digunakan di tapak penjajaannya.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen atau  pembantunya yang tidak mematuhi\nperenggan (1) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nLarangan penjualan makanan tidak selamat\n31. (1) Seseorang pemegang lesen tidak boleh menjual atau menawarkan untuk\njualan apa-apa makanan yang tidak selamat untuk dimakan oleh manusia.\n\n(2) Perbadanan boleh menyiasat, memeriksa dan menyita mana -mana\nmakanan yang tidak selamat untuk dimakan oleh manusia dan boleh me ngarahkan\nmakanan itu dimusnahkan dengan serta merta.\n\n(3) Pemegang lesen tidak berhak untuk menuntut apa -apa pampasan\ndaripada Perbadanan untuk mana -mana makanan yang disita oleh Perbadanan\ndi bawah perenggan (2).\n\n(4) Walau apa pun perenggan (2) dan (3),  mana-mana pemegang lesen yang\nmelanggar perenggan (1) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nPetak menjaja tidak boleh diserah hak, dipajak, disewa atau disewa kecil\n32. (1) Seseorang p emegang lesen tidak boleh menyerah  hak, memajak,\nmenyewa atau menyewa kecil petak yang diperuntukkan kepadanya  kepada\nmana-mana orang.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perenggan (1) melakukan\nsuatu kesalahan.\n\nPerubahan barang yang telah dilesenkan\n33. (1) Tiada pemegang lesen boleh menjual atau mempamerkan untuk jualan\napa-apa barang selain daripada barang yang telah ditetapkan dalam lesen kecuali\nmendapat kelulusan bertulis daripada Perbadanan.\n\n(2) Sesuatu permoh onan untuk mendapatkan kelulusan di bawah\nperenggan (1) hendaklah dibuat secara bertulis dalam bentuk dan cara yang ditentukan\noleh Perbadanan dan Perbadanan boleh, menurut budi  bicaranya, meluluskan atau\ntidak meluluskan permohonan itu.\n\n(3) Walau apa pun perenggan (2), mana-mana pemegang lesen yang\nmelanggar perenggan (1) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nWaktu menjalankan aktiviti penjajaan\n34. (1) Perbadanan boleh mengarahkan aktiviti penjajaan di mana -mana tapak\nmenjaja dijalankan  dalam tempoh dan waktu yang ditetapkan oleh Perbadanan dan\npemegang lesen hendaklah mematuhi arahan itu.\n\n(2) Perbadanan boleh mempertimbangkan sesuatu permohonan dari pada\npemegang lesen untuk melanjutkan tempoh dan w aktu yang telah ditetapkan oleh\nPerbadanan di bawah perenggan (1) setelah menerima permohonan secara bertulis\ndaripada pemegang lesen.\n\n(3) Walau apa pun perenggan (2), mana -mana pemegang lesen yang\nmelanggar perenggan (1) melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nBekalan air\n35. (1) Seseorang p emegang lesen tidak boleh menggunakan mana -mana air\nselain daripada air dari pada bekalan air awam dan tidak boleh menggunakan air paip\ndaripada mana-mana tandas bagi menjalankan aktiviti penjajaannya.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perenggan (1) melakukan\nsuatu kesalahan.\n\nPerobohan, penyitaan dan tuntutan\n36. (1) Walau apa pun undang-undang kecil 22, Perbadanan boleh menurut budi\nbicaranya—\n\n(a) menyita, memindah dan menahan apa -apa barang, kenderaan,\nperkakas atau gerai yang berhubungan dengan aktiviti penjaj aan\nseseorang yang tidak mempunyai lesen di bawah Undang -Undang\nKecil ini; atau\n\n(b) meroboh mana -mana gerai, petak peraga dinding, kajang, atap\natau struktur kepunyaan mana-mana penjaja tanpa lesen.\n\n(2) Perbadanan boleh melupuskan  barang-barang dari pada jenis mudah\nrosak dengan serta merta dengan apa-apa cara yang difikirkan sesuai oleh Perbadanan.\n\n(3) Mana-mana orang ya ng barang, kenderaan,  perkakas atau gerainya telah\ndisita dan ditahan di bawah perenggan (1) hendaklah menuntu t barang, kenderaan,\nperkakas atau gerai nya dalam tempoh yang diberikan oleh Perbadanan tertakluk\nkepada pembayaran apa -apa fi yang ditetapkan oleh Perbadanan dalam Jadual Ketiga\ndan jika tidak ada tuntutan dibuat dalam tempoh yang diberikan, barang, kenderaan,\nperkakas atau gerai itu akan dilupuskan mengikut ap a-apa cara yang ditetapkan oleh\nPerbadanan.\n\n(4) Perbadanan tidak akan bertanggungjawab untuk apa -apa barang,\nkenderaan, perkakas atau gerai yang telah disita dan dilupuskan di bawah\nundang-undang kecil ini.\n\n(5) Mana-mana orang yan g barang, kenderaan, perkakas atau gerai nya yang telah\ndisita, di tahan atau dilupuskan di bawah undang -undang k ecil ini tidak berhak\nmenuntut apa-apa pampasan daripada Perbadanan.\n\nKacau ganggu\n37. (1) Seseorang p emegang les en tidak boleh,  semasa menjalankan aktiviti\npenjajaannya, membuat atau menyebabkan  atau memb enarkan berlakunya  apa-apa\nkacau ganggu.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang melanggar perenggan (1) melakukan\nsuatu kesalahan.\n\nKuasa untuk menghendaki maklumat\n38. (1) Bagi maksud mengesan punca dan mencegah merebaknya apa -apa\njangkitan, Perbadanan boleh menghendaki pemegang lesen untuk memberi apa -apa\nmaklumat atau mengemukakan untuk pemeriksaan apa-apa dokumen, buku atau rekod\nberhubungan dengan pembantunya.\n\n(2) Mana-mana pemegang lesen yang enggan memberi apa -apa maklumat\natau mengemukakan apa-apa dokumen, buku atau rekod melakukan suatu kesalahan.\n\nPengecualian\n39. Perbadanan boleh , sama ada dengan atau tanpa syarat,  mengecualikan\nmana-mana pemegang lesen dari pada mana-mana peru ntukan Undang -Undang\nKecil ini.\n\nPenalti\n40. Mana-mana orang  yang melanggar mana -mana peruntukan Undang -Undang\nKecil ini mel akukan suatu kesalahan dan  boleh, apabila disabitkan, dikenakan denda\ntidak melebihi dua ribu ringgit atau pe menjaraan tidak melebihi satu tahun atau\nkedua-duanya, dan dalam hal suatu kesalahan yang berterusan, boleh dikenakan denda\ntidak melebihi dua ratus ringgit bagi tiap-tiap hari kesalahan itu berterusan se lepas\ndisabitkan.\n\nPembatalan dan peruntukan peralihan\n41. (1) Undang-Undang Kecil Majlis Perbandaran Labuan (Penjaja) 1968\n[G.N.L. 11 Tahun 1968] dibatalkan.\n\n(2) Apa-apa lesen yang dikeluarkan atau kelulusan yang diberikan di bawah\nUndang-Undang Kecil yang dibatalkan sebelum Undang-Undang Kecil ini mula berkuat\nkuasa hendaklah terus berkuat kuasa sepenuhnya sehingga lesen itu habis tempoh,\ndipinda, digantung atau dibatalkan, atau kelulusan itu habis tempoh atau dibatalkan\ndi ba wah Undang -Undang Kecil yang dibatalkan, yang hanya bagi maksud itu\nUndang-Undang Kecil yang dibatalkan hendaklah terus berkuat kuasa dan berkesan\nsepenuhnya.\n\n(3) Mana-mana prosiding yang belum selesai atau yang telah dimulakan\ndi bawah Undang-Undang Kecil yang dibatalkan sebelum Undang-Undang Kecil ini mula\nberkuat kuasa hendaklah diteruskan dan diselesaikan di bawah Undang -Undang Kecil\nyang dibatalkan seolah-olah Undang-Undang Kecil ini tidak dibuat.\n\nJADUAL PERTAMA\n [Undang-undang kecil 7]\n\nFI LESEN PENJAJA\n\nBil. Jenis Penjaja Fi Lesen\n1.  Penjaja bergerak RM48.00 setahun\n2.  Penjaja statik : Makanan RM10.00 sebulan\n3.  Penjaja statik : Selain daripada makanan RM15.00 sebulan\n4.  Penjaja Sementara : Satu petak RM15.00 sebulan\nRM0.50 sehari\n5.  Pasar Malam RM1.00 sehari\n\nJADUAL KEDUA\n [Undang-undang kecil 17(3) dan 19(2)]\n\nFI\n\nBil. Perkara Fi Yang Kena Dibayar\n1. Pelantikan penama RM5.00\n2. Pemindahan tapak menjaja RM10.00\n\nJADUAL KETIGA\n[Undang-undang kecil 36(3)]\n\nBil. Perkara Fi Yang Kena Dibayar\n1. Memindahkan barang/kenderaan/pekakas/gerai RM10.00\n2. Menyimpan barang/kenderaan/perkakas/gerai RM5.00 bagi tempoh tidak\nmelebihi daripada 7 hari\ndan RM1.00 sehari\nkemudian daripadanya.\n\nDibuat  9 November 2016\n[PL/PUU/100-1/6 Jld. 18 (5); PN(PU2)328A/XXIX]\n\nDATUK ROZMAN BIN DATUK HAJI ISLI\nPengerusi Perbadanan Labuan\n\nDisahkan 21 November 2016\n[KWP(S): 24/907/88 Jld. 8(5); PN(PU2)328A/XXIX]\n\n   DATUK SERI TENGKU ADNAN BIN TENGKU MANSOR\n Menteri Wilayah Persekutuan\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT ACT 1976\n\nLICENSING OF HAWKERS\n(FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2016\n\nARRANGEMENT OF BY-LAWS\n\nPART I\nPRELIMINARY\nBy-law\n\n1.  Citation and commencement\n2.  Interpretation\n\nPART II\nLICENSING\n\n3.  Licence required for hawking activity\n4.  Application for licence\n5.  Disqualification\n6.  Form of licence\n7.  Licence fee\n8.  Deposit\n9.  Replacement licence\n10.  Transfer of licence\n11.  Renewal of licence\n12.  Revocation of licence\n\nPART III\nGENERAL PROVISIONS\n\n13.  Contents of licence\n14.  Prohibitions\n\nBy-law\n\n15.  Medical examination and basic course in food preparation\n16.  Obligations of the licensee\n17.  Appointment of nominee\n18.  Employment of assistant\n19.  Licence shall be in respect of  specific hawking site\n20.  Size of stall, wall showcase and cart\n21.  Construction of awning or cover over pitch\n22.  Demolition and seizure\n23.  Prohibitions on hawking activity\n24.  Placing and moving of stall\n25.  Vehicles\n26.  Itinerant hawker\n27.  Persons prohibited from handling food\n28.  Method of handling food\n29.  Places where food preparation is prohibited\n30.  Sanitary requirements\n31.  Prohibition on sale of unwholesome food\n32.  Hawking pitch not to be assigned, leased, let out or sublet\n33.  Change of goods licensed\n34.  Operating hours for hawking activity\n35.  Water supply\n36.  Demolition, seizure and claims\n37.  Nuisance\n38.  Power to require information\n39.  Exemption\n40.  Penalty\n41.  Revocation and transitional provisions\nFIRST SCHEDULE\nSECOND SCHEDULE\nTHIRD SCHEDULE\n\nLOCAL GOVERNMENT ACT 1976\n\nLICENSING OF HAWKERS\n(FEDERAL TERRITORY OF LABUAN) BY-LAWS 2016\n\nIN exercise of the power  conferred by paragraph 73(1)(g) of the\nLocal Government Act 1976 [ Act 171 ] (as extende d and modified by the Federal\nTerritory of Labuan (Extension and Modification of Local Government Act 1976)\nOrder 2010 [ P.U. (A) 439/2010 ]), the  Perbadanan Labuan makes, and pur suant to\nsection 103 of the Act, the Minister confirms, the following by-laws:\n\nPART I\nPRELIMINARY\n\nCitation and commencement\n1. (1) These by-laws may be cited as the Licensing of Hawkers\n(Federal Territory of Labuan) By-Laws 2016.\n\n(2) These By-laws comes into operation on 1 January 2017.\n\nInterpretation\n2. In these By-laws, unless the context otherwise requires—\n\n\"hawking activity \" means the selling or offering  for sale  any goods at a\nhawking site;\n\n\"goods\" includes any type of food, services rendered or any other type of goods;\n\n\"licence fee\" means the prescribed payment rate for a licence issued under these\nBy-laws as specified in the First Schedule;\n\n\"stall\" means a structure erected for the purpose of hawking on which or in\nwhich goods are sold or displayed for sale at a hawking site;\n\n\"vehicle\" means a van, cart or any other vehicle approved by the Perbadanan to\nbe used for the purpose of hawking;\n\n\"food\" includes every goods manufactured, sold or represented for use as food or\ndrink for human consumption or which is used in the compo sition, preparation and\npreservation of any food or drink for human consumption and includes confectionery,\nchewing materials and any other ingredient of such  food, beverage, confectionery or\nchewing substances;\n\n\"licensee\" means any person to whom a hawke r licence is issued under these\nBy-laws;\n\n\"hawker\" means an itinerant hawker, temporary hawker or static hawker\nlicensed under these By-laws;\n\n\"itinerant hawker\" means any person who with or without a vehicle goes from\nplace to place on any road to sell or display for sale any goods;\n\n\"temporary hawker\" means any person who sells or displays for sale any goods\nat a stall or pitch identified on any road for that purpose by the Perbadanan for such\nperiod and according to the business hour as may be determined by the Perbadanan;\n\n\"static hawker\" means any person who sells or displays for sale any goods at a\nstall or pitch on any road or at any wall showcase;\n\n\"food preparation\" or \"preparing food\" includes handling, serving or selling food;\n\n\"Perbadanan\" means the Perbadanan Labuan as a statutory body established\nunder section 3 of the Perbadanan Labuan Act 2001 [Act 609];\n\n\"equipment\" includes containers, utensils, chairs, tables, equipment or any other\nthing used in connection with hawking activity;\n\n\"pitch\" means any space marked out by the Perbadanan at a hawking site to\noperate the hawking activity;\n\n\"wall showcase\" means a structure approved by the Perbadanan which is erected\non or against any part of any wall of a building;\n\n\"hawking site \" means any building, road or area where hawking activity  is\npermitted by the Perbadanan on the day or time specified by the Perbadanan.\n\nPART II\nLICENSING\n\nLicence required for hawking activity\n3. (1) Any person may carry out activities as a hawker when a hawker licence is\nissued by the Perbadanan under these By-laws.\n\n(2) Any person who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nApplication for licence\n4. (1) Subject to by-law 3, an application for a licence under these By -laws shall\nbe made in such form and manner as determined by the Perbadanan.\n\n(2) The Perbadanan may approve or not approve an application for a licence\nunder these By-laws.\n\n(3) The Perbadanan may, if it thinks necessary, require any applicant to\nattend in person to furnish any  document or further information regarding an\napplication for a licence.\n\n(4) A licence issued under these By-laws shall be subject to—\n\n(a) the licence period as determined by the Perbadanan;\n\n(b) the tenancy agreement of the hawking site signed by the applican t,\nif the Perbadanan thinks necessary;\n\n(c) the provisions of these By -laws, conditions and restrictions\nimposed by the Perbadanan and by any relevant authorities;\n\n(d) payment of deposit as provided in by-law 8;\n\n(e) payment of a licence fee as prescribed in the First Schedule; and\n\n(f) any other requirements under any relevant laws.\n\n(5) The Perbadanan may, from time to time and while a licence is still in\nforce, impose any additional conditions on the licence or amend or revoke any condition\nimposed on the licence.\n\n(6)  A written notice shall be given to the licensee before the Perbadanan\nmakes any decision under paragraph (5).\n\nDisqualification\n5. Notwithstanding by-law 4, no licence shall be issued under these By-laws to any\nperson who is—\n\n(a) a non-citizen of Malaysia; or\n\n(b) under the age of eighteen years old.\n\nForm of licence\n6. A licence issued under these By -laws shall be in any form as may be determined\nby the Perbadanan.\n\nLicence fee\n7. (1) The licence fee payable for the issuance of a licen ce under these By -laws\nis as prescribed in the First Schedule.\n\n(2) The Perbadanan may exempt any licensee from the liability of paying the\nwhole or any part of the licence fee.\n\n(3) The licence fee paid under paragraph (1) shall not be refundable.\n\nDeposit\n8. (1) The Perbadanan may require any person to whom a licence is issued to\npay a deposit of an amount of money not exceeding fifty thousand ringgit to ensure that\nthe provisions of the Act, By-laws, conditions or restrictions of the licence are observed.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Perbadanan may, if it thinks\nnecessary, exempt any licensee from the liability of paying the whole or any part of the\ndeposit.\n\n(3) If there is a breach of any provision s of the Act, By -laws, conditions or\nrestrictions of the licence, the Perbadanan shall give a notice to the licensee within the\ntime specified in the notice to give representation as to why his deposit shall not be\nforfeited.\n\n(4) The Perbadanan may, after considering the representation given by the\nlicensee or if the licensee fails to make a representation, decides either to forfeit the\nwhole or part of the deposit.\n\n(5) Subject to paragraph (4), the Perbadanan may require the licensee to\nreplenish the whole or part of the deposit that has been forfeited.\n\n(6) The deposit paid shall, unless forfeited, be refunded to the licensee\nwithout any adjustment for interest on the amount deposited under paragraph (1) after\nthe licensee has ceased operating the hawking activity at his hawking site.\n\n(7) The licen see shall inform the Perbadanan if he has ceased operating the\nhawking activity at his hawking site.\n\n(8) Notwithstanding paragraph (7), the licensee shall apply to the\nPerbadanan within thirty days from the date he has ceased operating the hawking\nactivity for his deposit to be refunded.\n\n(9) If the licensee does not apply for his deposit to be refunded or the deposit\nis not claimed within the period specified in paragraph (8), the deposit shall be forfeited\nand shall be paid into the Perbadanan Labuan Fun d and shall form part of the revenue\nof the fund.\n\nReplacement licence\n9. If the Perbadanan is satisfied that any valid licence issued under these By -laws is\nlost, defaced or damaged, the Perbadanan may issue a replacement licence.\n\nTransfer of licence\n10. (1) No licensee shall transfer his licence to any other party.\n\n(2) Any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nRenewal of licence\n11. (1) A licence issued under these By -laws shall not be renewed as a right and\nan application for renewal of a licence shall be deemed as an application for a licence.\n\n(2) An application for renewal of a licence shall be made within sixty days\nbefore the expiry of the licence and shall be made in such form and manner as may be\ndetermined by the Perbadanan.\n\n(3) The Perbadanan may, if it thinks necessary, require any applicant to\nattend in person to furnish any  document or further information regarding an\napplication to renew a licence.\n\n(4) The Perbadanan may renew or not renew a licence and shall inform t he\napplicant of its decision in writing or by any other manner as may be determined by the\nPerbadanan and to refund the deposit to the applicant subject to by-law 8(9).\n\n(5) A licence if renewed under paragraph (4) shall be subject to—\n\n(a) the licence period as determined by the Perbadanan;\n\n(b) payment of a licence fee as prescribed in the First Schedule;\n\n(c) the provisions of these By -laws, conditions and restrictions\nimposed by the Perbadanan and by any relevant authorities;\n\n(d) the licensee does not have any rental arrears for his hawking site;\nand\n\n(e) the tenancy agreement is still in force.\n\n(6) No further deposit need to be given by the licensee if his licence is\nrenewed.\n\n(7) The Perbadanan shall not be responsible to pay any compensation to the\nlicensee if the licence is not renewed under paragraph (4).\n\nRevocation of licence\n12. (1) The Perbadanan may r evoke a licence issued under  by-law 4 if it  is\nsatisfied that—\n\n(a) the licensee has contravened any provision s of these Act, By -laws,\nconditions or restrictions of the licence;\n\n(b) the licensee has, either in relati on to the application of a licence or\nat any time after the licence is issued, submitted to the Perbadanan\n\na document or declaration which is false, confusing or not\naccurate; or\n\n(c) the licensee has not  operated the licensed hawking activity  for a\nconsecutive period of three months without informing the\nPerbadanan.\n\n(2) The r evocation of a licence under  paragraph (1) may be made by the\nPerbadanan without any payment of compensation to the licensee  and the Perbadanan\nmay forfeit the whole deposit paid under by-law 8.\n\n(3) Before a licence  is revoked, the Perbadanan shall give a notice in writing\nto the licensee requiring him to make a representation within the period as specified in\nthe notice as to why his licence shall not be revoked.\n\n(4) After the expiry of the period s pecified in the notice under paragraph (3)\nand after considering the licensee's representation or if the licensee fails to make a\nrepresentation, the Perbadanan shall proceed to consider such matter and inform its\ndecision in a written notice to the licensee.\n\n  (5) If the Perbadanan decides to revoke the licence, the revocation of the\nlicence shall take effect on the date specified in the notice served to the licensee.\n\n (6) Any licensee who  operates a hawking activity after his license is revoked\nunder paragraph (5) commits an offence.\n\nPART III\nGENERAL PROVISIONS\n\nContents of licence\n13. A licence issued by the Perbadanan to a licensee under these By -laws shall\ncontain the following particulars:\n\n(a) the name, recent address and identity card number of the licensee;\n\n(b) a recent passport size photograph of the licensee;\n\n(c) the type of hawker;\n\n(d) the validity period of licence;\n\n(e) the type of goods to be sold;\n\n(f) the name, recent address, identity card number  and recent passport size\nphotograph of the assistant employed by the licensee, if any;\n\n(g) period and time of hawking;\n\n(h) hawking site; and\n\n(i) any other conditions and restrictions imposed by the Perbadanan.\n\nProhibitions\n14. (1) No licensee shall—\n\n(a) employ any person who is under the age of eighteen years old;\n\n(b) employ any foreign person;\n\n(c) allow any gambling or immoral activities or permit any conduct\nwhich will cause a nuisance, disturbance, injury or noisiness to the\nresidents within the surrounding area of hawking site; and\n\n(d) operate other activities at the hawking site other than the hawking\nactivity specified in his licence.\n\n(2) Any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nMedical examination and basic course in food preparation\n15. (1) Any person who is involved in food preparation for hawking activity\nshall—\n\n(a) undergo a medical examination as the Perbadanan may direct;\n\n(b) be inoculated against any infectious diseases; and\n\n(c) attend a basic course for food prepa ration recognised by the\nMinistry of Health Malaysia.\n\n(2) The medical examination and inoculation against any infectious disease s\nshall be carried out by a medical or health officer registered under the Medical Act 1971\n[Act 50].\n\n(3) The licensee shall—\n\n(a) comply with the requirement s of paragraph (1) if the licensee\nhimself is involved in food preparation for hawking activity; and\n\n(b) ensure that  his nominee appointed under  by-law 17  and his\nassistant employed under  by-law 18 involved in food preparat ion\ncomply with the requirements under paragraph (1).\n\n(4) Any licensee who fails to comply with paragraph (3) commits an offence.\n\n(5) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), any person who is involved in food\npreparation for hawking activity may be directed by the Perbadanan at any time to—\n\n(a) undergo a medical examination;\n(b) be inoculated against any infectious diseases; and\n\n(c) attend a basic course relating to food preparation.\n\n(6) Any person who fails to comply with paragraph (5) commits an offence.\n\nObligations of the licensee\n16. (1) A licensee shall at all times be present to conduct or monitor his hawking\nactivity.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), if the licensee cannot be present to\nconduct his hawking activity for a period of thirty days or more, he shall—\n\n(a) appoint a nominee under by-law 17 to replace him; or\n\n(b) temporarily close the pitch allocated to him.\n\n(3) Any licensee who contravenes paragraphs (1) and (2) commits an offence.\n\nAppointment of nominee\n17. (1) An application for a nominee under by-law 16(2)(a) shall be made in such\nform and manner as determined by the Perbadanan.\n\n(2) The Perbadanan may—\n\n(a) require the licensee to submit  further information for the purpose\nof considering the application; or\n\n(b) approve the application sub ject to  other condition s or refuse the\napplication.\n\n(3) The fee payable by the licensee for the application for the appointment of\na nominee shall be as prescribed in the Second Schedule.\n\n(4) A nominee appointed under  paragraph (2) shall be subject to th ese\nBy-laws, conditions and restrictions imposed by the Perbadanan to the licensee and is\nliable in the same manner as a licensee.\n\nEmployment of assistant\n18. (1) A licensee shall not employ any person as an assistant without the prior\nwritten approval of the Perbadanan.\n\n(2) An application for an approval under paragraph (1) shall be made in such\nform and manner as determined by the Perbadanan.\n\n(3) The Perbadanan may—\n\n(a) require the licensee to submit  further information for the purpose\nof considering the application; or\n\n(b) approve the application subject to  other conditions or refuse the\napplication.\n\n(4) The employment of an assistant shall not exempt the licensee from\nby-law 16(1).\n\n(5) Any assistant employed under paragraph (4) is subject to—\n\n(a) the provision s of these By-laws, conditions and restrictions\nimposed by the Perbadanan under by-law 4(4); and\n\n(b) any other conditions prescribed by the Perbadanan under\nsubparagraph 3(b).\n\n(6) Notwithstanding this by-law, any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1)\ncommits an offence.\n\nLicence shall be in respect of specific hawking site\n19. (1) A licence issued under  by-law 4 shall be in respect of a designated\nhawking site as specified in the licence.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding paragraph (1), the Perbadanan, may in its discretion\nupon an application made by a licensee , allow the transfer of a hawking site to anot her\nhawking site to sell similar goods subject to—\n\n(a) the payment of a fee as prescribed in the Second Schedule;\n\n(b) the licens ee does not have any rental arrears f or the original\nhawking site;\n\n(c) the licensee has signed a tenancy agreement for the use of another\nhawking site, if the Perbadanan thinks necessary; and\n\n(d) other directions as may be determined by the Perbadanan.\n\n(3) The Perbadanan may, if it deems necessary and appropriate, give notice in\nwriting to the licensee to transfer the hawking site allocated to him to another hawking\nsite within the period determined by the Perbadanan in the notice.\n\n(4) Any licensee who fails to  comply with the notice under paragraph (3)\ncommits an offence.\n\n(5) The licensee whose hawking site has been transferred under\nparagraph (3) is not entitled to claim any compensation from the Perbadanan.\n\nSize of stall, wall showcase and cart\n20. (1) The maximum size for a stall is 5 metres long and 3 metres wide except\nstalls built by the Perbadanan.\n\n(2) No wall showcase shall exceed 4 metres long by 2 metres high by 1 metre\nwide.\n\n(3) The cart used by an itinerant hawker shall n ot exceed 2 metres long\nand 1 metre wide and the cover or awning over it shall not extend more than 1 metre\nbeyond any part of the cart.\n\n(4) Any licensee who contravenes this by-law commits an offence.\n\nConstruction of awning or cover over pitch\n21. (1) No awning or any type of cover or structure shall be put up at any\nhawking site, unless permitted by the Perbadanan, subject to any conditions as the\nPerbadanan thinks necessary.\n\n(2) The construction of an awning or cover or struct ure permitted under\nparagraph (1) shall be in accordance with the conditions imposed by the Perbadanan.\n\n(3) The permission given under paragraph (1) may be withdrawn at any time\nby the Perbadanan, upon being notified in writing of non -compliance of any of the\nconditions imposed u nder paragraph (1) and the licensee shall demolish the awning,\ncover or structure within the period specified by the Perbadanan in the notice.\n\n(4) If the licensee fails to comply with the notice under  paragraph (3), the\nPerbadanan may demolish the awning,  cover or structure and the Perbadanan may\nrecover the expenses incurred by the Perbadanan for the demolishing works from the\nlicensee.\n\n(5) The Perbadanan shall not be liable to pay any compensation to the\nlicensee for actions taken under this by-law.\n\n(6) Any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1) or (2) commits an offence.\n\nDemolition and seizure\n22. (1) The Perbadanan may giv e notice in writing to any  licensee to demolish\nany stall, wall showcase, awning, cover or structure over any stall or pitch\nconstructed—\n\n(a) which does not comply with the size specified in by-law 20; or\n\n(b) without the permission of the Perbadanan,\n\nwithin the period specified by the Perbadanan in the notice.\n\n(2) If the licensee fails to c omply with the notice under  paragraph (1), the\nPerbadanan, after the expiry of the period specified in the notice , may take steps to\ndemolish the stall, wall showcase, awning, cover or structure on the pitch without\npaying any compensation to the licensee and the Perbadanan may claim the\ndemolishing cost from the licensee.\n\n(3) The Perbadanan may seize any vehicle used for a hawking activity\nwithout the approval of the Perbadanan or a cart used by any licensee which is not in\naccordance with the size for the cart to be used for hawking activity under by-law 20(3).\n\n(4) Any licensee may claim the vehicle or cart s eized under  paragraph (3)\nwithin the period determined by the Perbadanan subject to by-law 36(3).\n\n(5) The Perbadanan shall not be liable for any damages and losses incurred\nby the licensee as a result of the actions taken by the Perbadanan under this by-law.\n\nProhibitions on hawking activity\n23. (1) No licensee shall operate his hawking activity—\n\n(a) within 9 metres of a street junction; or\n\n(b) within 3.6 metres of a fire hydrant.\n\n(2) No licensee shall operate his hawking activity  in suc h manner as to\nobstruct or to interfere with the free flow of vehicular traffic and the free movement of\npedestrians.\n\n(3) No licensee or his assistant shall use a loudhailer, loudspeaker,\nmicrophone or any other instrument for intensifying sound in the course of his hawking\nactivity.\n\n(4) Any licensee who contravenes this by-law commits an offence.\n\nPlacing and moving of stall\n24. (1) A licensee shall comply with such verbal or written directions given by\nthe Perbadanan from time to time with regard to the placing of his stall, goods  or other\nequipment relating to his hawking activity at any hawking site.\n\n(2) A temporary hawker shall remove his stall, vehicle, goods and other\nequipment relating to his hawking activity when the period and time of hawking end.\n\n(3) Any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1) or (2) commits an offence.\n\nVehicles\n25. (1) A licensee who uses a vehicle for the purpose of hawking activity  shall\nensure the vehicle is in accordance with the size or sha pe as determined by the\nPerbadanan.\n\n(2) Any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nItinerant hawker\n26. (1) An itinerant hawker other than an itinerant hawker who uses a van shall\nbe continuously on the move except when engaged in the selling of goods to customers.\n\n(2) An itinerant hawker using a van shall operate his hawking activity at the\npitch permitted by the Perbadanan within the period and time specified in the licence\nand shall remove his van from the pitch when the period and time of hawking end.\n\n(3) No itinerant hawker using a van shall place or display for sale any goods\nused for or related to his hawking activity outside the van.\n\n(4) Any itinerant hawker who contravenes this by-law commits an offence.\n\nPersons prohibited from handling food\n27. (1) Any person who is suffering from or carrying any communicable disease\nshall not be engaged in food preparation for hawking activity.\n\n(2) Any person who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nMethod of handling food\n28. (1) Any licensee or his assistant involved in food preparation—\n\n(a) shall ensure that the food offered for sale is clean and safe to eat\nand drink;\n\n(b) shall use tongs, scoops, plastic gloves or other suitable utensil for\nfood preparation;\n\n(c) shall not use his fingers to touch any other parts of his body during\nfood preparation;\n\n(d) shall not use his breath to open any bag or wrapper used for the\nsale of food;\n\n(e) shall not wipe his hands with his clothing or by any means other\nthan with a clean towel or cloth;\n\n(f) shall not cough or sneeze near any food;\n\n(g) shall not smoke;\n\n(h) shall keep himself and his clothes in a clean condition and shall at\nall times wear an apron, a head cover and such other things as\ndirected by the Perbadanan from time to time;\n\n(i) does not have cuts or skin abrasions on his hands or fingers; and\n\n(j) shall use a clean towel for the purpose of wiping or cleaning any\npackage or articles used for the food preparation.\n\n(2) Any licensee or his assistant who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an\noffence.\n\nPlaces where food preparation is prohibited\n29. (1) A licensee or his assistant shall not prepare food—\n\n(a)  in any toilet or bathroom;\n\n(b)  in any place where any thing or animal is allowed to be or kept; or\n\n(c) in any place where the f ood is likely to be contaminated or\nbecomes polluted or cleanliness of the food will be affected.\n\n(2) Any licensee or his assistant who contravenes  paragraph (1) commits an\noffence.\n\nSanitary requirements\n30. (1) A licensee and his assistant shall ensure that—\n\n(a) any type of food for sale is sold and prepared on a surface with the\nheight of 0.5 meters above the ground or floor;\n\n(b) the hawking site is maintained so as to be in a clean condition at all\ntimes;\n\n(c) the surrounding areas which is immediately in front of, behind and\nbeside the  hawking site assigned to the licensee are in a clean\ncondition;\n\n(d) the food offered for sale  shall be in a clean condition and covered\nwith a food cover at all times;\n\n (e) the vehicles used for hawking or transporting  food for sale  are\nalways in a clean condition;\n\n(f)  the equipment and fixtures used in the hawking activity shall be in\na clean condition;\n\n(g) only containers or packing tools as determined or permitted by the\nPerbadanan is used to wrap up food for sale;\n\n(h) the food for customers is not  wrapped in unclean paper or paper\nwith writing or printed matter on it or with material which might\ncontaminate the food;\n\n(i) all equipment used in his hawking activity  must be kept in a\nproper place and in a clean condition;\n\n(j) the licensee and his assistant  shall always wear clean clothes and\nshall also wear an apron and a cap;\n\n(k) litter bins  of any type and  size as determined  by the Perbadanan\nare sufficiently provided;\n\n(l) all garbage is collected and  packed in plasti c bag s and placed in\nsealed containers provided for that purpose,  and shall ensure the\ncontainers are emptied  and cleaned as often as necessary  for the\npurpose of cleanliness at all times;\n\n(m) paper or material that is not clean shall not be used for the packing\nof goods;\n\n(n) the packaging or containers used  for packing  fruit and vegetable\nshall not be made  from materials that will contaminate or change\nthe colour or taste of the fruit  or vegetable, or cause the fruit or\nvegetable to be in a condition that is injurious to health; and\n\n(o) any poison  or any  harmful substance or any  other material that\nmay pollute the  good condition  of the goods for  sale shall not  be\nused in his hawking site.\n\n(2) Any licensee or his assistant who fails to comply with  paragraph (1)\ncommits an offence.\n\nProhibition on sale of unwholesome food\n31. (1) A licensee shall not sell or offer for sale any unwholesome food for human\nconsumption.\n\n(2) The Perbadanan may investigate, inspect and seize any  food which is\nunwholesome for human consumption and  may direct the food to be destroyed\nimmediately.\n\n(3) The licensee  is not entitled  to claim any  compensation from the\nPerbadanan for any food seized by the Perbadanan under paragraph (2).\n\n(4) Notwithstanding paragraphs (2) and (3), any licensee who contravenes\nparagraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nHawking pitch not to be assigned, leased, let out or sublet\n32. (1) A licensee shall not assign, lease, let out or sublet  the pitch allocated to\nhim to any person.\n\n(2) Any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nChange of goods licensed\n33. (1) No licensee shall sell or display for sale any goods other than the goods\nspecified in the licence except with the written approval of the Perbadanan.\n\n(2) An application for an  approval under paragraph (1) shall be in writing  in\nsuch form and  manner determined by the Perbadanan and the Perbadanan may, at its\ndiscretion, approve or not approve the application.\n\n(3) Notwithstanding paragraph (2), any licensee who contravenes\nparagraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nOperating hours for hawking activity\n34. (1) The Perbadanan may direct hawking activity  at any hawking site  to be\noperated within the period  and time as specified by the Perbadanan and the licensee\nshall comply with such directions.\n\n(2) The Perbadanan may consider an application from the licensee to  extend\nthe period and time for hawking specified by the Perbadanan under paragraph (1) upon\nreceiving an application in writing from the licensee.\n\n(3) Notwithstanding paragraph (2), any licensee who  contravenes\nparagraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nWater supply\n35. (1) A licensee shall not use any water other than water from a  public water\nsupply and shall not use the pipe d water from any toilet  for the op eration of his\nhawking activity.\n\n(2) Any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nDemolition, seizure and claims\n36. (1) Notwithstanding by-law 22, the Perbadanan may at its discretion—\n\n(a) seize, remove and detain any  goods, vehicle, equipment or stall\nrelating to  the hawking activity  of a person  who is not licensed\nunder these By-laws; or\n\n(b) demolish any  stall, wall showcase, awning, cover or structure\nbelonging to any unlicensed hawker.\n\n(2) The Perbadanan may dispose of goods of a perishable nature immediately\nby any means deemed appropriate by the Perbadanan.\n\n(3) Any person whose goods, vehicle, equipment or stall has been seized and\ndetained under paragraph (1) shall claim the goods, vehicle, equipment or stall within\nthe period given by the Perbadanan subject to the payment of any fee prescribed by the\nPerbadanan in the Third Schedule and if no claim is  made within the period  provided,\nsuch goods, vehicle, equipment or stall will be disposed of in  such manner  as may be\ndetermined by the Perbadanan.\n\n(4) The Perbadanan shall not be liable  for any goods , vehicle, equipment or\nstall which has been seized and disposed of under this by-law.\n\n(5) Any person  whose goods, vehicle, equipment or stall  has been seized,\ndetained or disposed o f under this by-law shall not be entitled to claim  any\ncompensation from the Perbadanan.\n\nNuisance\n37. (1) A licensee shall not, during the operation of his hawking activity, create or\ncause or allow any nuisance to occur.\n\n(2) Any licensee who contravenes paragraph (1) commits an offence.\n\nPower to require information\n38. (1) For the purpose of tracing the source and preventing the sp read of any\ninfection, the Perbadanan may require a licensee to furnish any information or produce\nfor inspection any document, book or record relating to his assistant.\n\n(2) Any licensee who refuses to give any information or produce any\ndocument, book or record commits an offence.\n\nExemption\n39. The Perbadanan may, conditionally or unconditionally, exempt any licensee from\nany provisions of these By-laws.\n\nPenalty\n40. Any person who contravenes any provisions of these By-laws commits an offence\nand shall, upon conviction, be liable to a fine not exceeding two thous and ringgit or to\nimprisonment not exceeding one year or to both , and in the case of a continuing offence\nto a fine not exceeding two hundred ringgit for each day during which the offence is\ncontinued after conviction.\n\nRevocation and transitional provisions\n41. (1) The Labuan Municipal Council (Hawkers) By -Laws 1968\n[G.N.L. 11 of 1968] is revoked.\n\n(2) Any licence issued or approval granted under the revoked By -laws before\nthe coming into operation of these By -laws shall continue in full force until the licence\nexpires, is amended, suspended or cancelled, or the approval expires or revoked under\n\nthe revoked By-laws, for which purpose only the revoked By-laws shall continue to be in\nfull force and effect.\n\n(3) Any proceedings pending or commenced under the revoked By -laws\nbefore the coming into operation of these By -laws shall be continued and concluded\nunder the revoked By-laws as if these By-laws has not been made.\n\nFIRST SCHEDULE\n [By-law 7]\n\nLICENCE FEE FOR HAWKERS\n\nNo. Type of Hawker Licence Fee\n1. Itinerant hawker RM48.00 per year\n2. Static hawker : Food RM10.00 per month\n3. Static hawker : Other than food RM15.00 per month\n4. Temporary Hawker : One Pitch RM15.00 per month\nRM0.50 per day\n5. Night market RM1.00 per day\n\nSECOND SCHEDULE\n [By-law 17(3) and 19(2)]\n\nFEE\n\nNo. Item Fee Payable\n1. Appointment of nominee RM5.00\n2. Transfer of hawking site RM10.00\n\nTHIRD SCHEDULE\n[By-law 36(3)]\n\nNo. Item Fee Payable\n1. Removing of any goods/vehicle/equipment/stall RM10.00\n2. Detaining of any goods/vehicle/equipment/stall RM5.00 for a period not\nexceeding 7 day s and\nRM1.00 per day thereafter.\n\nMade 9 November 2016\n[PL/PUU/100-1/6 Jld. 18 (5); PN(PU2)328A/XXIX]\n\nDATUK ROZMAN BIN DATUK HAJI ISLI\nChairman of the Perbadanan Labuan\n\nConfirmed 21 November 2016\n[KWP(S): 24/907/88 Jld. 8(5); PN(PU2)328A/XXIX]\n\nDATUK SERI TENGKU ADNAN BIN TENGKU MANSOR\nMinister of Federal Territories"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4746"] = {"id":"MY-H4746","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2017&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2017年护照（摩洛哥公民签证豁免）令","en":"PASSPORTS (EXEMPTION OF VISA TO CITIZEN OF MOROCCO) ORDER 2017","orig":"PASSPORTS (EXEMPTION OF VISA TO CITIZEN OF MOROCCO) ORDER 2017","ms":"Perintah Pasport (Pengecualian Visa kepada Warganegara Maghribi) 2017","vi":"Lệnh về Hộ chiếu (Miễn thị thực cho công dân Maroc) năm 2017","th":"คำสั่งหนังสือเดินทาง (การยกเว้นวีซ่าสำหรับพลเมืองโมร็อกโก) ค.ศ. 2017","id":"Perintah Paspor (Pembebasan Visa bagi Warga Negara Maroko) Tahun 2017"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2017","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2017_P.U.(A)344-2017_PASSPORTS (EXEMPTION OF VISA TO CITIZEN OF MOROCCO) ORDER 2017.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4746-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Pasport (Pengecualian Visa\n\nkepada Warganegara Maghribi) 2017.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 15 November 2017.\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H4746-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Menteri mengecualikan warganegara Maghribi daripada kehendak visa di bawah\n\nsubseksyen 2(1) Akta tertakluk kepada syarat yang berikut:\n\n(a) warganegara Maghribi itu hendaklah memiliki pasport diplomatik,\n\npasport perkhidmatan, pasport khas atau pasport biasa yang sah;\n\n(b) warganegara Maghribi itu hendaklah dikeluarkan Pas Lawatan (Sosial)\n\nyang sah bagi tempoh sembilan puluh hari bagi setiap kemasukan;\n\n(c) warganegara Maghribi itu tidak dibenarkan untuk memohon apa-apa\n\npas lain di bawah Peraturan-Peraturan Imigresen 1963\n\n[L.N. 228/1963]; dan\n\n(d) warganegara Maghribi itu hendaklah memasuki dan keluar dari Malaysia\n\nhanya melalui pos kawalan imigresen, tempat mendarat yang\n\ndibenarkan, lapangan terbang yang dibenarkan atau pintu masuk yang\n\ndibenarkan sebagaimana yang diwartakan di bawah subseksyen 5(1)\n\nAkta Imigresen 1959/63 [Akta 155].\n\nDibuat 10 November 2017\n\n[KDN.IM.S.600-8/13/51 (45); PN(PU2)482/II]\n\nDATO' SERI DR. AHMAD ZAHID BIN HAMIDI\n\nMenteri Dalam Negeri\n\nPASSPORTS ACT 1966\n\nPASSPORTS (EXEMPTION OF VISA TO CITIZEN OF MOROCCO) ORDER 2017\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 4 of the Passports Act 1966 [Act 150],\n\nthe Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4747"] = {"id":"MY-H4747","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2018&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":null,"en":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (MALAYSIA-SINGAPORE SECOND CROSSING BRIDGE AND EXPRESSWAY AND PERLING EXPRESSWAY) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 2) O","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (MALAYSIA-SINGAPORE SECOND CROSSING BRIDGE AND EXPRESSWAY AND PERLING EXPRESSWAY) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 2) O","ms":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (MALAYSIA-SINGAPORE SECOND CROSSING BRIDGE AND EXPRESSWAY AND PERLING EXPRESSWAY) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 2) O"},"level":"law","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2018","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2018_P.U.(A)344-2018_FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (MALAYSIA-SINGAPORE SECOND CROSSING BR.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4747-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Jalan-Jalan Persekutuan\n\n(Pengurusan Persendirian) (Pungutan Tol) (Jambatan dan Lebuh Raya Laluan\n\nKedua Malaysia-Singapura dan Lebuh Raya Perling) (Pindaan) (No. 2) 2018.\n\n(2) Perintah ini disifatkan telah mula berkuat kuasa pada 13 Februari 2018.\n\nPenggantian Jadual Kedua"}},{"id":"MY-H4747-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Jalan-Jalan Persekutuan (Pengurusan Persendirian) (Pungutan Tol)\n\n(Jambatan dan Lebuh Raya Laluan Kedua Malaysia-Singapura dan Lebuh Raya\n\nPerling) 1998 [P.U. (A) 97/1998] dipinda dengan menggantikan Jadual Kedua dengan\n\nJadual yang berikut:\n\n\"JADUAL KEDUA\n\n[Subperenggan 2(1)]\n\nKADAR TOL BAGI TEMPOH DARI 13 FEBRUARI 2018 HINGGA 31 DISEMBER 2018\n\n(1)\n\nKelas Kenderaan\n\n(2)\n\nTol Kena Dibayar\n\n(RM)\n\nPlaza\n\nTol A\n\nKompleks\n\nSultan\n\nAbu\n\nBakar\n\nPlaza Tol Tanjung Kupang Plaza\n\nTol\n\nLima\n\nKedai\n\nPlaza Tol\n\nPerling\n\nMasa Puncak\n\n5.01 pagi – 10.00 pagi\n\n3.01 petang – 11.00 malam\n\nLuar Masa Puncak\n\n10.01 pagi – 3.00 petang\n\n11.01 malam – 5.00 pagi\n\nLebuh Raya Jambatan\n\n0 Kenderaan\n\ndengan dua\n\ngandar dan\n\ndua roda\n\n2.20 - 1.10 1.10 bagi laluan terus\n\nmelalui lebuh raya dan\n\njambatan dan pusingan U\n\n- -\n\n1 Kenderaan\n\ndengan dua\n\ngandar dan\n\ntiga atau\n\nempat roda\n\n(kecuali teksi\n\ndan bas)\n\n10.60 2.20 5.30 4.00 bagi laluan terus\n\nmelalui lebuh raya dan\n\njambatan dan pusingan U\n\n3.90 2.30\n\n2 Kenderaan\n\ndengan dua\n\ngandar dan\n\nlima atau\n\nenam roda\n\n(kecuali bas)\n\n27.40 3.40 13.70 4.50 bagi laluan terus\n\nmelalui lebuh raya dan\n\njambatan dan pusingan U\n\n7.80 4.60\n\n3 Kenderaan\n\ndengan tiga\n\ngandar atau\n\nlebih\n\n(kecuali bas)\n\n54.80 6.90 27.40 6.10 bagi laluan terus\n\nmelalui lebuh raya dan\n\njambatan dan pusingan U\n\n9.80 5.70\n\n4 Teksi 9.20 1.10 4.60 3.00 bagi\n\nlaluan terus\n\nmelalui lebuh\n\nraya dan\n\njambatan\n\n2.20 bagi\n\npusingan\n\nU\n\n2.00 1.10\n\n(1)\n\nKelas Kenderaan\n\n(2)\n\nTol Kena Dibayar\n\n(RM)\n\nPlaza\n\nTol A\n\nKompleks\n\nSultan\n\nAbu\n\nBakar\n\nPlaza Tol Tanjung Kupang Plaza\n\nTol\n\nLima\n\nKedai\n\nPlaza Tol\n\nPerling\n\nMasa Puncak\n\n5.01 pagi – 10.00 pagi\n\n3.01 petang – 11.00 malam\n\nLuar Masa Puncak\n\n10.01 pagi – 3.00 petang\n\n11.01 malam – 5.00 pagi\n\nLebuh Raya Jambatan\n\n5 Bas 14.60 1.80 7.30 4.50 bagi\n\nlaluan terus\n\nmelalui lebuh\n\nraya dan\n\njambatan\n\n3.60 bagi\n\npusingan\n\nU\n\n3.90 2.30\n\nDibuat 20 Disember 2018\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/1 Jld.19; PN(PU2)426/LXVI]\n\nBARU BIAN\n\nMenteri Kerja Raya\n\n\".\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) ACT 1984\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS)\n\n(MALAYSIA-SINGAPORE SECOND CROSSING BRIDGE AND EXPRESSWAY AND\n\nPERLING EXPRESSWAY) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 2) ORDER 2018\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 2 of the\n\nFederal Roads (Private Management) Act 1984 [Act 306], the Minister makes the\n\nfollowing order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4748"] = {"id":"MY-H4748","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2019&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2019年合作社（马来西亚伊赫蒂亚尔友好信托合作社有限公司）（豁免）令","en":"CO-OPERATIVE SOCIETIES (KOPERASI SAHABAT AMANAH IKHTIAR MALAYSIA BERHAD) (EXEMPTION) ORDER 2019","orig":"CO-OPERATIVE SOCIETIES (KOPERASI SAHABAT AMANAH IKHTIAR MALAYSIA BERHAD) (EXEMPTION) ORDER 2019","ms":"Perintah Koperasi (Koperasi Sahabat Amanah Ikhtiar Malaysia Berhad) (Pengecualian) 2019","vi":"Lệnh về Hợp tác xã (Hợp tác xã Sahabat Amanah Ikhtiar Malaysia Berhad) (Miễn trừ) năm 2019","th":"คำสั่งสหกรณ์ (สหกรณ์ซาฮาบัตอามานะห์อิคเทียรมาเลเซียเบอร์ฮัด) (การยกเว้น) ค.ศ. 2019","id":"Perintah Koperasi (Koperasi Sahabat Amanah Ikhtiar Malaysia Berhad) (Pembebasan) Tahun 2019"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2019","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2019_P.U.(A)344-2019_CO-OPERATIVE SOCIETIES (KOPERASI SAHABAT AMANAH IKHTIAR MALAYSIA BERHAD) (EXEMPTION) ORDER 2019.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4748-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Koperasi (Koperasi Sahabat\nAmanah Ikhtiar Malaysia Berhad) (Pengecualian) 2019.\n\n (2) Perintah ini disifatkan telah mula berkuat kuasa pada 30 September 2018.\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H4748-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Koperasi Sahabat Amanah Ikhtiar Malaysia Berhad dikecualikan daripada\npemakaian subseksyen 43(4) Akta bagi maksud pelantikan anggota Lembaga Koperasi\nSahabat Amanah Ikhtiar Malaysia Berhad pada mesyuarat agung perwakilan tahunan bagi\nsesi 2018/2019.\n\nDibuat 28 November 2019\n[MED.(S)100-1/11/8 Jld. 3 (7); PN(PU2)527/XIX]\n\n        DATUK SERI MOHD REDZUAN BIN MD. YUSOF\n           Menteri Pembangunan Usahawan\n\nCO-OPERATIVE SOCIETIES ACT 1993\n\nCO-OPERATIVE SOCIETIES (KOPERASI SAHABAT AMANAH IKHTIAR MALAYSIA\nBERHAD) (EXEMPTION) ORDER 2019\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 87 of the Co-operative Societies Act 1993\n[Act 502], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4749"] = {"id":"MY-H4749","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2020&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2020年联邦道路（西马来西亚）（修正）（第10号）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (WEST MALAYSIA) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 10) ORDER 2020","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (WEST MALAYSIA) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 10) ORDER 2020","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Semenanjung Malaysia) (Pindaan) (Bilangan 10) 2020","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Malaysia Barat) (Sửa đổi) (số 10) năm 2020","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (มาเลเซียตะวันตก) (การแก้ไข) (ฉบับที่ 10) ค.ศ. 2020","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Malaysia Barat) (Perubahan) (Nomor 10) Tahun 2020"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2020","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2020_P.U.(A)344-2020_FEDERAL ROADS (WEST MALAYSIA) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 10) ORDER 2020.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4749-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Jalan Persekutuan\n\n(Malaysia Barat) (Pindaan) (No. 10) 2020.\n\n(2) Perintah ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 10 Disember 2020.\n\nPindaan Jadual Pertama"}},{"id":"MY-H4749-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Jalan Persekutuan (Malaysia Barat) 1989 [P.U. (A) 401/1989] dipinda\n\ndalam Jadual Pertama—\n\n(a) di bawah kepala \"Negeri Perak\"—\n\n(i) dengan menggantikan butiran 21 dengan butiran yang berikut:\n\n\"21. (Laluan 109): Jalan Bota Kanan-Kampung Gajah-Teluk Intan\n\nDari persimpangan Laluan 58, Jalan Bidor-Teluk Intan di koordinat\n\nU 4.007645, T 101.037826 dan berakhir di persimpangan Laluan 5,\n\nJalan Jelapang-Ipoh-Ayer Tawar di koordinat\n\nU 4.353854, T 100.880957 di dalam sempadan hak lalu-lalang\n\nsebagaimana yang ditunjukkan dalam PETA 13: JALAN-JALAN\n\nPERSEKUTUAN NEGERI PERAK (jarak sepanjang 51.967 km).\"; dan\n\n(ii) dengan memasukkan selepas butiran 29 butiran yang berikut:\n\n\"30. (Laluan 322): Jambatan Kg. Lambor\n\nDari persimpangan Laluan 109, Jalan Bota Kanan-Kampung\n\nGajah- Teluk Intan di koordinat U 4.270178, T 100.903950 dan\n\nberakhir di persimpangan Laluan A18, Jalan Bota Kiri-Jambatan\n\nDato Sagor di koordinat U 4.270780, T 100.896455 di dalam sempadan\n\nhak lalu-lalang sebagaimana yang ditunjukkan dalam\n\nPETA 14: JALAN-JALAN PERSEKUTUAN NEGERI PERAK\n\n(jarak sepanjang 0.835 km).\"; dan\n\n(b) dengan memasukkan selepas PETA 12: JALAN-JALAN PERSEKUTUAN\n\nNEGERI PERAK peta yang berikut:\n\n\"PETA 13: JALAN-JALAN PERSEKUTUAN NEGERI PERAK\n\nU 4.353854\n\nT 100.880957\n\nU 4.007645\n\nT 101.037826\n\nPETUNJUK:\n\nJALAN YANG DIWARTAKAN\n\nSEBAGAI JALAN PERSEKUTUAN\n\nJALAN PERSEKUTUAN\n\nJALAN NEGERI\n\nNOMBOR LALUAN\n\nPanjang jalan\n\nyang diwartakan\n\n= 51.967 km\n\nPETA 14 : JALAN-JALAN PERSEKUTUAN NEGERI PERAK\n\nA18\n\n\".\n\nU 4.270178\n\nT 100.903950\n\nU 4.270780\n\nT 100.896455\n\nSungai Perak\n\nPanjang Jalan yang\n\nDiwartakan = 0.835 km\n\nPETUNJUK:\n\nJALAN YANG DIWARTAKAN\n\nSEBAGAI JALAN PERSEKUTUAN\n\nJALAN PERSEKUTUAN\n\nJALAN NEGERI\n\nNOMBOR LALUAN\n\nA18\n\nDibuat 8 Disember 2020\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/6/10 Jld.3(46); PN(PU2)391/XXXIX]\n\nDATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\n Menteri Kanan Kerja Raya\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut seksyen 4 Akta Jalan Persekutuan 1959]\n\nFEDERAL ROADS ACT 1959\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (WEST MALAYSIA) (AMENDMENT) (NO. 10) ORDER 2020\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 3 of the\n\nFederal Roads Act 1959 [Act 376], the Minister, after consultation with the\n\nState Government of Perak, makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H475"] = {"id":"MY-H475","coverage":"full","language":"en","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-detail.php?act=606&lang=BI","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":57,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2000年光盘法","en":"OPTICAL DISCS ACT 2000","orig":"OPTICAL DISCS ACT 2000","vi":"Luật về Đĩa quang năm 2000","th":"พระราชบัญญัติแผ่นดิสก์แสง ค.ศ. 2000","id":"Undang-Undang Cakram Optik Tahun 2000","ms":"Akta Cakera Optik 2000"},"level":"law","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"ACT606","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2000","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 57 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2000_606_OPTICAL DISCS ACT 2000.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H475-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"en":"1. (1) This Act may be cited as the Optical Discs Act 2000.\n(2) This Act shall come into operation on a date to be appointed\n\nby the Minister by notification in the Gazette, and the Minister\nmay appoint different dates for different provisions of this Act.\n\nInterpretation"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"en":"2. (1) In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires—\n\"article\" includes device, contrivance, machine or equipment;\n\n\"Assistant Controller\" means an Assistant Controller of Optical\nDiscs appointed under section 3;\n\n\"code of conduct\" means the code of conduct issued under\nsection 22;\n\n\"Controller\" means the Controller of Optical Discs appointed\nunder section 3;\n\nPengori ul telut petai\n\n\"copyright\" has the meaning assigned to it by the Copyright\nAct 1987 (Act 332);\n\n\"Deputy Controller\" means a Deputy Controller of Optical Discs\nappointed under section 3:\n\n\"infringing copy\" has the meaning assigned to it by the Copyright\nAct 1987;\n\n\"licence\" means a licence granted under section 7;\n\n\"licensed premises\" means any premises specified in a licence\nin which optical discs are authorised to be manufactured;\n\n\"licensee\" means a person to whom a licence is granted under\nsection 7;\n\n\"manufacture\" means the processes and activities involved in\nthe manufacturing of optical discs, including mastering or replicating\nor both;\n\n\"‘manufacturer's code\" means the manufacturer's code assigned\nto a licensee under paragraph 7(2)(b);\n\n\"Minister\" means the Minister responsible for domestic trade\nand consumer affairs;\n\n\"optical disc\" means—\n(a) any medium or device listed in Schedule 1; or\n(b) any other medium or device on which data may be stored\n\nin digital form and read by means of a laser,\n\nand includes any such medium or device manufactured for any\npurpose, whether or not any data readable by means of a laser or\nany other means has been stored on it;\n\n\"owner of copyright\" means the owner of copyright within the\nmeaning of the Copyright Act 1987;\n\n\"place\" means any area on land or water and includes any\nbuilding, structure or enclosure, whether moveable or not;\n\nOptical Discs                                        9\n\n\"prescribed\" means prescribed by regulations made under this\nAct;\n\n\"register\" means the register kept by the Controller under this\nAct;\n\n\"this Act\" includes any regulation made under this Act.\n\n(2) For the purpose of this Act, a person is engaged in the\nmanufacture of optical discs if he owns, directs, manages or\notherwise has control of a business which undertakes the manufacture\nof optical discs.\n\nPart II\n\nCONTROLLER OF OPTICAL DISCS, ETC.\nAppointments of Controller, etc."}},{"id":"MY-H475-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"chapter":{"en":"Part II"},"text":{"en":"3. (1) The Minister may appoint, from amongst public officers,\na Controller of Optical Discs, such number of Deputy Controllers\nof Optical Discs, Assistant Controllers of Optical Discs and other\nofficers as may be necessary for the purposes of this Act.\n\n(2) The Controller shall, subject to the general direction and\ncontrol of the Minister, perform the functions and duties imposed\nand may exercise the powers conferred upon him under this Act.\n\n(3) The Deputy Controllers, Assistant Controllers and other\nofficers appointed under subsection (1) shall be under the direction\nand control of the Controller.\n\n(4) The Controller and the Deputy Controllers may perform all\nthe functions and duties imposed and may exercise all the powers\nconferred upon an Assistant Controller under this Act.\n\n(5) A Deputy Controller may perform all the functions and\nduties imposed and may exercise all the powers conferred upon\nthe Controller under this Act except the powers under Part III.\n\n(6) Notwithstanding subsection (5), the Controller may delegate\nto a Deputy Controller any of his powers under Part III, and when\nso delegated such power shall be exercised by the Deputy Controller\n\nunder the control of and subject to such directions and restrictions\nas may be specified by the Controller.\n\n(7) A delegation under subsection (6) may be revoked at any\ntime by the Controller and shall not prevent the Controller from\nhimself exercising the delegated powers.\n\n(8) All officers appointed under this section shall be deemed to\nbe public servants within the meaning of the Penal Code (Act\n574].\n\nPart III\n\nLICENSING, ETC.\n\nLicence to manufacture optical discs"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"4. Any person who manufactures optical discs without a valid\nlicence under this Act commits an offence.\n\nUnlicensed premises"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"5. A licensee who manufactures optical discs in a place other\nthan the licensed premises commits an offence.\n\nApplication for licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"6. (1) An application for a licence under this Act shall be made\nin writing to the Controller in such form, and shall be accompanied\nby such documents or information, as may be prescribed.\n\n(2) Where a person proposes to manufacture optical discs at\nmore than one place, he may make one application for a licence\nin respect of all those places.\n\n(3) The Controller may, at any time after receiving the\napplication under subsection (1) and before it is determined, by\na written notice require the applicant to provide such additional\ndocuments or information as the Controller deems necessary.\n\n(4) Where any additional document or information required\nunder subsection (3) is not provided by the applicant within the\n\nOptical Discs                                      11\n\ntime specified in the notice or any extension thereof granted by\nthe Controller, the application shall be deemed to be withdrawn\nand shall not be further proceeded with, but without prejudice to\na fresh application being made by the applicant.\n\n(5) An application under this section may be withdrawn at any\ntime before it is granted or refused.\n\nGrant or refusal of a licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A7","no":7,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 7"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"7. (1) Upon receipt of an application together with the documents\nand information required under section 6, the Controller may grant\nthe licence or refuse to grant the licence.\n\n(2) If the Controller grants a licence under subsection (1), he\nshall—\n\n(a) require the licensee to pay the prescribed fees within the\nprescribed period;\n\n(b) assign to the licensee a manufacturer's code which shall\nconsist of—\n\n(i) one or more letters or numbers;\n(ii) a mark, sign, symbol or device; or\n(iii) any combination of letters, numbers, marks, signs,\nsymbols or devices,\nas may be prescribed;\n\n(c) impose such conditions as he thinks fit for the purpose\nof—\n\n(i) preventing the manufacture of infringing copies of\nworks in which copyright subsists; and\n\n(ii) protecting the rights of owners of copyright and\nother persons to whom rights are conferred under\nthe Copyright Act 1987; and\n\n(d) impose such other conditions as he deems fit.\n(3) A licence shall be deemed to have not been granted if the\n\nfees required under paragraph (2)(a) are not paid within the\nprescribed period.\n\n(4) Where the Controller refuses to grant a licence, he shall\nimmediately notify the applicant in writing of his refusal without\nassigning any reason for the refusal.\n\n(5) Where the Controller grants a licence in respect of the\napplication made under subsection 6(2), the Controller shall issue\na separate licence for each place of manufacture.\n\nValidity of licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A8","no":8,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 8"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"8. The licence granted under section 7, unless sooner revoked or\nsuspended, shall be valid for such period as may be specified in\nthe licence.\n\nPower to vary conditions"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A9","no":9,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 9"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"9. (1) The Controller may, at any time after a licence is granted—\n(a) impose any new or additional conditions on the licence;\n(b) vary or revoke any condition imposed on the licence; or\n(c) vary or revoke any condition already varied under\nparagraph (b).\n(2) Where the Controller proposes to take an action under\nsubsection (1), he shall give the licensee—\n(a) a written notice of his intention; and\n\n(b) an opportunity to make written representations within\nfourteen days from the date of service of the notice.\n\n(3) After the expiry of the period of fourteen days, and after\nconsidering any representation made by the licensee, the Controller\nshall decide whether to impose, vary or revoke any condition\nunder subsection (1) or to take no further action.\n\n(4) The Controller shall give the licensee a written notice of\nhis decision under subsection (3).\n\nOptical Discs                                      13\n\nRevocation of licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A10","no":10,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 10"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"10. (1)\nthat—\n(a)\n\n(b)\n\n(c)\n\n(d)\n\n(e)\n\nThe Controller may revoke a licence if he is satisfied\n\nthe licensee has failed to comply with any obligation\nimposed upon him under this Act;\n\nthe licensee has contravened any of the conditions of\nthe licence, or any provision of this Act, regardless of\nthe fact that there has been no prosecution for an offence\nin respect of such contravention;\n\nthe licensee has been convicted of an offence under this\nAct;\n\nthe licensee or any person who is or is to be a director,\nmanager, secretary or other similar officer of the licensee\nhas, either in connection with the application for the\nlicence, or at any time after the grant of the licence,\nprovided false or misleading or inaccurate information\nto the Controller; or\n\nthe licensee has ceased to carry on the business of\nmanufacturing optical discs.\n\n(2) Before revoking a licence, the Controller shall give the\nlicensee a notice in writing of his intention to do so and require\nthe licensee to show cause within fourteen days as to why the\nlicence should not be revoked.\n\n(3) After the expiry of the period of fourteen days and after\nconsidering any representations made by the licensee, the Controller\nshall decide whether to revoke the licence or to take no further\n\naction.\n\n(4) The Controller shall give the licensee written notice of his\ndecision under subsection (3).\n\n(5) The revocation of a licence shall take effect—\n\n(a)\n\n(b)\n\nwhere there is no appeal against such revocation, on the\nexpiration of fourteen days from the date on which the\nnotice of revocation is served on thé licensée; or\n\nwhere there is an appeal against such revocation, when\nthe revocation is confirmed by the Minister.\n\nSurrender of licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A11","no":11,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 11"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"11. (1) A licensee may surrender his licence by forwarding it to\nthe Controller with a written notice of its surrender.\n\n(2) The surrender shall take effect on the date the Controller\nreceives the licence and the notice under subsection (1) or where\na later date is specified in the notice, on that later date.\n\nEffect of revocation, surrender or expiry of licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A12","no":12,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 12"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"12. Upon the revocation of a licence under section 9 or its surrender\nunder section 10 taking effect, or upon the expiry of the licence,\nthe licensee shall immediately cease to manufacture optical discs.\n\nTransfer of licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A13","no":13,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 13"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"13. (1) A licence is not transferable except with the approval of\nthe Controller.\n\n(2) A licensee who transfers his licence to another person without\nthe approval of the Controller commits an offence.\n\n(3) The Controller may approve the transfer of the licence\nif—\n\n(a) the licensee dies or becomes incapacitated or a bankrupt;\n\n(b) in the case of a company, the licensee is wound up or\na receiver or manager is appointed in respect of the\nbusiness of the licensee; or\n\n(c) for any reason the Controller is satisfied it would be\nunjust not to transfer the licence.\n\n(4) An application for the transfer of a licence shall be made\nin writing to the Controller.\n\nRenewal of licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A14","no":14,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 14"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"14. A licensee shall apply to the Controller for the renewal of a\nlicence not less than one month before the date of the expiry of\nthe existing licence.\n\nOptical Discs                                        15\n\nDisplay of licence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A15","no":15,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 15"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"15. (1) A licensee shall at all times display his licence in a\nconspicuous place at his licensed premises.\n\n(2) A licensee who contravenes subsection (1) commits an\noffence.\n\nRegister"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A16","no":16,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 16"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"16. (1) The Controller shall establish and maintain a register in\nsuch form as may be prescribed of the licences granted under this\nAct.\n\n(2) The Controller shall make the register available for public\ninspection subject to such conditions as he thinks fit.\n\nMaintenance of records"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A17","no":17,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 17"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"17. (1) A licensee shall keep and maintain a proper records in\nsuch form and containing such information as may be prescribed,\nconcerning the operation of his business in relation to the\nmanufacture of optical discs.\n\n(2) The records shall be—\n\n(a) kept solely for the purpose of entering the records required\nunder this Act;\n\n(b) available at all times for the examination of any Assistant\nController; and\n\n(c) kept up to date and in good order and condition.\n\n(3) A licensee shall submit the records and furnish other relevant\ndocuments and information as and when required by the Controller\nwithin such time as may be specified by the Controller, except\nwhere any trade secret would be disclosed if the document or\ninformation is so furnished.\n\n(4) A licensee who contravenes subsection (1), (2) or (3) commits\nan offence.\n\nAppeal"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A18","no":18,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 18"},"chapter":{"en":"Part III"},"text":{"en":"18. (1) Any person who is aggrieved by any decision of the\nController under this Part may appeal to the Minister in the\nprescribed manner within one month from the date the decision is\ncommunicated to such person.\n\n(2) The Minister may confirm, reverse or vary the decision of\nthe Controller appealed against.\n\n(3) The decision of the Minister under subsection (2) shall be\nfinal.\n\nPart IV\n\nMANUFACTURER'S CODE\n\nOptical discs to be marked with manufacturer's code"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A19","no":19,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 19"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV"},"text":{"en":"19. (1) A licensee shall cause each optical disc manufactured\nby him to be marked with the manufacturer's code assigned to\nhim under paragraph 7(2)(b).\n\n(2) A licensee who contravenes subsection (1) commits an\noffence.\n\n(3) In this section, \"marked\" means to be marked in accordance\nwith the standards prescribed under section 20.\n\nMarking standards"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A20","no":20,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 20"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV"},"text":{"en":"20. (1) The Minister may prescribe standards for the marking\nof the manufacturer's code on optical discs.\n\n(2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the Minister\nmay prescribe—\n\n(a) different standards in relation to different classes or\ndescriptions of optical discs; or\n\n(b) standards relating to the manner in which, and the means\nby which, manufacturer's code are to be marked on optical\ndiscs or on optical discs of any class or description.\n\nOptical Discs                                       17\n\nApplying false manufacturer's code"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A21","no":21,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 21"},"chapter":{"en":"Part IV"},"text":{"en":"21. (1) Any person who—\n(a) forges a manufacturer's code;\n\n(b) falsely applies to an optical disc a manufacturer's code\nor any mark so resembling a manufacturer's code as to\nbe calculated to deceive;\n\n(c) makes any die, block, machine or other instrument for\nthe purpose of forging, or which is capable of being\n3               used for forging, a manufacturer's code;\n\n(d) disposes of or has in his possession any die, block, machine\nor other instrument for the purpose of forging a\nmanufacturer's code; or\n\n(e) causes to be done anything referred to in paragraph (a),\n\n(b), (c) or (d),\n\ncommits an offence.\n\n(2) In any proceedings for an offence under subsection (1), it\nshall be a defence for the person charged to prove that he acted\nwithout intent to deceive or defraud.\n\nPart V\n\nCODE OF CONDUCT\n\nController may issue code of conduct"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A22","no":22,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 22"},"chapter":{"en":"Part V"},"text":{"en":"22. (1) The Controller may issue a code of conduct dealing with\nthe conduct of any person connected with the business of\nmanufacturing optical discs.\n\n(2) The Controller may, before issuing a code of conduct under\nsubsection (1), consult with such body representing the persons\nto whom the code of conduct will apply and other interested persons\nas he thinks fit.\n\n(3) The code of conduct issued by the Controller under subsection\n(1) shall be published in the Gazette.\n\nRevocation, etc., of code of conduct"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A23","no":23,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 23"},"chapter":{"en":"Part V"},"text":{"en":"23. (1) The Controller may revoke, amend or revise, whether in\nwhole or in part, a code of conduct if he is satisfied that the code\nof conduct, whether in whole and in part, is no longer consistent\nwith the provisions of this Act.\n\n(2) The Controller may, before revoking, amending or revising\na code of conduct, consult with such body representing the persons\nto whom the code of conduct applies and other interested persons\nas he thinks fit.\n\n(3) The provisions of the code of conduct revoked, amended\nor revised by the Controller under subsection (1) shall be published\nin the Gazette.\n\nCivil penalty for non-compliance"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A24","no":24,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 24"},"chapter":{"en":"Part V"},"text":{"en":"24. (1) Notwithstanding Part VI, a person who fails to comply\nwith any provisions of a code of conduct shall be liable to pay to\nthe Controller a fine not exceeding two hundred ringgit.\n\n(2) Notwithstanding the provisions of any other written law,\nthe fine payable under this section may, without prejudice to any\nother remedy or sanction, be recoverable as a civil debt.\n\nCompliance with code of conduct a legal defence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A25","no":25,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 25"},"chapter":{"en":"Part V"},"text":{"en":"25. Compliance with a code of conduct shall be a defence against\nany prosecution, action or proceedings of any nature, whether in\na court or otherwise, taken against a person who is subject to the\ncode of conduct regarding a matter dealt with in that code of\nconduct.\n\nPART VI\n\nOFFENCES AND PENALTY\n\nPenalty"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A26","no":26,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 26"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"26. (1) Any person who commits an offence under Part III except\nunder section 15 shall on conviction be liable—\n\n(a) if such person is a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding\nfive hundred thousand ringgit, and for a second or\n\n(b)\n\nOptical Discs                                      19\n\nsubsequent offence to a fine not exceeding one million\nringgit; or\n\nif such person is not a body corporate, to a fine not\nexceeding two hundred and fifty thousand ringgit or to\nimprisonment for a term not exceeding three years or to\nboth, and for a second or subsequent offence to a fine\nnot exceeding five hundred thousand ringgit or to\nimprisonment for a term not exceeding six years or both.\n\n(2) Where a person being a director, manager, secretary or\nother similar officer of a body corporate is guilty of an offence\nunder subsection (1) by virtue of section 30, he shall on conviction\nbe liable to the penalty provided for in paragraph (1)(b).\n\nOffences with respect to information"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A27","no":27,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 27"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"27. (1)\n\nAny person who submits false or misleading information\n\nin any application, report or other document for any purpose under\nthis Act commits an offence and shall on conviction be liable—\n\n(a)\n\n(b)\n\nif such person is a body corporate, to a fine not exceeding\nfive hundred thousand ringgit, and for a second or\nsubsequent offence to a fine not exceeding one million\nringgit; or\n\nif such person is not a body corporate, to a fine not\nexceeding two hundred and fifty thousand ringgit or to\nimprisonment for a term not exceeding three years or to\nboth, and for a second or subsequent offence to a fine\nnot exceeding five hundred thousand ringgit or to\nimprisonment for a term not exceeding six years or both.\n\n(2) Any person who—\n\n(a)\n\n(b)\n\nfurnishes or causes to be furnished to any Assistant\nController or police officer not below the rank of Inspector\nany false or misleading particular, information or statement\nin respect of any matter which such officer requires to\nbe given under this Act;\n\nrefuses to answer or gives a false answer to any question\nput to him by any Assistant Controller or police officer\nnot below the rank of Inspector for the purpose of obtaining\nany particulars, information or statement required to be\ngiven under this Act; or\n\n(c) fails or refuses to produce any document as may be\nrequired by any Assistant Controller or police officer\nnot below the rank of Inspector,\n\ncommits an offence.\n\n(3) Where a person being a director, manager, secretary or\nother similar officer of a body corporate is guilty of an offence\nunder subsection (1) by virtue of section 30, he shall on conviction\nbe liable to the penalty provided for in paragraph (1)(b).\n\n(4) Nothing in this section shall be construed as requiring a\nperson to answer any question or to give any information if the\nanswer or information would have a tendency to expose him to a\ncriminal charge, penalty or forfeiture.\n\nDisappearance or destruction of article, efc., to be seized"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A28","no":28,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 28"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"28. Any person who causes the disappearance or destruction of\nany article, optical disc, thing, book or document liable to be\nseized under this Act with the intent to prevent the seizure thereof\ncommits an offence.\n\nDisclosure of confidential information"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A29","no":29,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 29"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"29. (1) Any person who makes use of or discloses to any other\nperson any confidential information obtained by virtue of the\nprovisions of this Act commits an offence.\n\n(2) Nothing in subsection (1) shall operate to prevent the\ndisclosure of information where the disclosure is made—\n\n(a) for or in connection with the due administration of this\nAct;\n(b) for the purpose of any legal proceedings;\n\n(c) for the purpose of any investigation conducted under\nthis Act;\n\n(d) to any person or any officer who is approved in writing\nby the Minister as a proper person to receive the\ninformation; or\n\n(e) for or in connection with the preparation by the\nGovernment of statistics in respect of the operation of\nthis Act.\n\nOptical Discs                     21\nOffences by director, manager, secretary, etc."}},{"id":"MY-H475-A30","no":30,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 30"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"30. Where any offence against any provision of this Act has\nbeen committed by a body corporate, any person who at the time\nof the commission of the offence was a director, manager, secretary\nor other similar officer of the body corporate or was purporting\nto act in any such capacity, or was in any manner or to any extent\nresponsible for the management of any of the affairs of such body\ncorporate, or was assisting in such management, shall also be\nguilty of that offence unless he proves that the offence was\ncommitted without his consent or connivance and that he exercised\nall such diligence to prevent the commission of the offence as he\nought to have exercised, having regard to the nature of his functions\nin that capacity and to all the circumstances.\n\nOffences by employee or agent"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A31","no":31,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 31"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"31. Where any person (\"the principal\") would be liable under\nthis Act to any punishment or penalty for any act, omission, neglect\nor default, he shall be liable to the same punishment or penalty\nfor every such act, omission, neglect of default of any employee\nor agent of his, or the employee of such agent, if such act, omission,\nneglect or default was committed by the principal's employee in\nthe course of his employment, or by the agent when acting on\nbehalf of the principal, or by the employee of such agent in the\ncourse of his employment by such agent or otherwise on behalf\nof the agent.\n\nObstruction of officers"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A32","no":32,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 32"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"32. Any person who obstructs, impedes, assaults or interferes\nwith any Assistant Controller or police officer not below the rank\nof Inspector in the performance of his functions under this Act\ncommits an offence.\n\nGeneral penalty"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A33","no":33,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 33"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"33. (1) Any person who commits an offence under this Act for\nwhich no penalty is expressly provided shall on conviction be\nliable to a fine not exceeding one hundred and fifty thousand\nringgit or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three years\nor to both, and for a second or subsequent offence he shall be\nliable to a fine not exceeding three hundred thousand ringgit or\nto imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years or to both.\n\n(2) Any body corporate which commits an offence under this\nAct for which no penalty is expressly provided shall on conviction,\nbe liable to a fine not exceeding two hundred and fifty thousand\nringgit, and for a second or subsequent offence it shall be liable\nto a fine not exceeding five hundred thousand ringgit.\n\n(3) Where a person being a director, manager, secretary or\nother similar officer of a body corporate is guilty of an offence\nunder this Act by virtue of section 30, and no penalty is expressly\nprovided for such offence, he shall be liable to the penalty provided\nfor in subsection (1).\n\nCompounding of offences"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A34","no":34,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 34"},"chapter":{"en":"PART VI"},"text":{"en":"34. (1) The Controller or a Deputy Controller or any person\nauthorised in writing by the Controller may with the consent of\nthe Public Prosecutor compound any offence under this Act which\nis prescribed to be a compoundable offence committed by any\nperson by making a written offer to such person to compound the\noffence upon payment to the Controller or the Deputy Controller\nor any person authorised in writing by the Controller of an amount\nnot exceeding fifty per centum of the amount of maximum fine\nfor that offence within such time as may be specified in the offer.\n\n(2) An offer under subsection (1) may be made at any time\nafter the offence has been committed, but before any prosecution\nfor it has been instituted, and where the amount specified in the\noffer is not paid within the time specified in the offer or within\nsuch extended period as the Controller or a Deputy Controller or\nany person authorised in writing by the Controller may grant,\nprosecution for the offence may be instituted at any time thereafter\nagainst the person to whom the offer was made.\n\n(3) Where an offence has been compounded under subsection\n(1)—\n\n(a) no prosecution shall thereafter be instituted in respect of\nsuch offence against the person to whom the offer to\ncompound was made; and\n\n(b) any article, optical disc, thing, book or document seized\nin connection with such offence shall be released\nimmediately, subject to such conditions as the Controller\nor Deputy Controller or any person authorised in writing\nby the Controller thinks fit to impose.\n\nOptical Discs                                             23\nPart VII\n\nENFORCEMENT\n\nPower of enforcement"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A35","no":35,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 35"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"35. (1) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector may exercise all the powers of enforcement\nunder this Act.\n\n(2) Every Assistant Controller or police officer, when acting\nagainst any person under this Act, shall declare his office and\nshall on demand produce to the person against whom he is acting\nsuch authority card as the Controller may direct to be carried by\nsuch Assistant Controller or as the Inspector General of Police\nmay direct to be carried by such police officer.\n\nPower of investigation"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A36","no":36,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 36"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"36. (1) Any Assistant Controller or a police officer not below\nthe rank of Inspector shall have the power to investigate any\noffence under this Act.\n\n(2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the Assistant Controller\nor police officer may issue orders to a licensee to further his\ninvestigation and secure compliance with this Act.\n\n(3) In addition to his powers under subsections (1) and (2), an\nAssistant Controller or a police officer not below the rank of\nInspector investigating an offence under this Act may exercise all\nor any of the powers in relation to police investigation in seizable\ncases given by the Criminal Procedure Code [Act 593].\n\nAdditional powers"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A37","no":37,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 37"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"37. Any Assistant Controller or police officer not below the rank\nof Inspector may, for the purpose of enforcing this Act, do all or\nany of the following:\n\n(a) visit, enter, inspect and examine with or without notice\nany licensed premises at any reasonable hour;\n\n(b) require the production of record, books, accounts,\ncomputerised data or documents kept by the licensee\nand inspect, examine and copy any of them;\n\n(c) require the production of any identification document\nfrom any person in relation to any case or offence under\nthis Act; or\n\n(d) make such inquiry as may be necessary to ascertain\nwhether the provisions of this Act have been complied\nwith.\n\nSearch by warrant"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A38","no":38,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 38"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"38. (1) If it appears to a Magistrate, upon written information\non oath and after such inquiry as he considers necessary, that\nthere is reasonable cause to believe that an offence under this Act\nis being or has been committed on any premises, the Magistrate\nmay issue a warrant authorising any Assistant Controller or police\nofficer not below the rank of Inspector named therein to enter the\npremises at any reasonable time by day or by night, with or without\nassistance and if need be by force.\n\n(2) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector may, in the premises entered under subsection\n(1), search and seize any article, optical disc, thing, book or\ndocument, including computerised data, which contain or is\nreasonably believed to contain information as to any offence\nsuspected to have been committed and is likely to disclose evidence\nof the commission of any offence under this Act.\n\n(3) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector conducting a search under subsection (1) may,\nif in his opinion it is reasonably necessary to do so for the purpose\nof investigating into the offence, search any person who is in or\non such premises but no female person shall be searched except\nby another female person.\n\n(4) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector entering any premises by virtue of this section\nmay take with him such other persons and such equipment as may\nappear to him necessary.\n\nOptical Discs                                      25\n\n(5) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector shall, on leaving any premises, if the premises\nare unoccupied or the occupier is temporarily absent, leave the\npremises as effectively secured against trespassers as he found\nthem.\n\n(6) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector making a search of a person under subsection\n(3) may seize, detain or take possession of any article, optical\ndisc, thing, book or document found on such person for the purpose\nof the investigation being carried out by such officer.\n\n(7) Where, by reason of its nature, size or amount, it is not\npracticable to remove any article, optical disc, thing, book or\ndocument, seized under this section, the seizing officer shall, by\nany means seal the article, optical disc, thing, book or document\nin the premises or container in which it is found.\n\n(8) A person who, without lawful authority, breaks, tampers\nwith or damages the seal referred to in subsection (7) or removes\nany article, optical disc, thing, book or document under seal or\nattempts to do so commits an offence.\n\nSearch and seizure without warrant"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A39","no":39,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 39"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"39. Where an Assistant Controller or a police officer not below\nthe rank of Inspector in any of the circumstances referred to in\nsection 38 has reasonable grounds for believing that by reason of\nthe delay in obtaining a search warrant under that section the\ninvestigation would be adversely affected or evidence of the\ncommission of an offence is likely to be tampered with, removed,\ndamaged or destroyed, the Assistant Controller or police officer\nnot below the rank of Inspector may enter the premises and exercise\nall the powers referred to in section 38 in as full and ample a\nmanner as if he were authorised to do so by a warrant issued\nunder that section.\n\nList of things seized"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A40","no":40,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 40"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"40. (1) Except as provided in subsection (2), where any article,\noptical disc, thing, book or document is seized under this Part,\nthe seizing officer shall prepare a list of the things seized and\n\nimmediately deliver a copy signed by him to the occupier of the\npremises which has been searched, or to his agent or servant, at\nthose premises.\n\n(2) Where the premises are unoccupied, the seizing officer\nshall whenever possible post a list of the things seized conspicuously\non the premises.\n\nWarrant admissible notwithstanding defects"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A41","no":41,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 41"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"41. A search warrant issued under this Act shall be valid and\nadmissible notwithstanding any defect, mistake or omission therein\nor in the application for such warrant and any article, optical disc,\nthing, book or document seized under such warrant shall be\nadmissible in evidence in any proceedings under this Act.\n\nAccess to computerised data"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A42","no":42,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 42"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"42. (1) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector conducting a search under this Act shall be\ngiven access to computerised data whether stored in a computer\nor otherwise.\n\n(2) In this section, \"access\" includes being provided with the\nnecessary password, encryption code, decryption code, software\nor hardware and any other means required to enable comprehension\nof computerised data.\n\nPower to require attendance of person acquainted with case"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A43","no":43,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 43"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"43. (1) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector making an investigation under this Act may by\norder in writing require the attendance before himself of any person\nwho appears to the Assistant Controller or a police officer not\nbelow the rank of Inspector to be acquainted with the facts and\ncircumstances of the case, and such person shall attend as so\nrequired.\n\n(2) If any person refuses to attend as so required, the Assistant\nController or police officer not below the rank of Inspector may\nreport such refusal to a Magistrate who shall issue a summons to\nsecure the attendance of such person as may be required by the\norder made under subsection (1).\n\nOptical Discs                                           27\n\nExamination of person acquainted with case"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A44","no":44,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 44"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"44. (1) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector making an investigation under this Act may\nexamine orally any person supposed to be acquainted with the\nfacts and circumstances of the case.\n\n(2) The person examined under subsection (1) shall be legally\nbound to answer all questions relating to such case put to him by\nthe Assistant Controller or police officer, but such person may\nrefuse to answer any question the answer to which would have a\ntendency to expose him to a criminal charge or penalty or forfeiture.\n\n(3) A person making a statement under this section shall be\nlegally bound to state the truth, whether or not such statement is\nmade wholly or partly in answer to the questions.\n\n(4) An Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the\nrank of Inspector examining a person under subsection (1) shall\nfirst inform that person of the provisions of subsections (2) and\n\n(3).\n\n(5) A statement made by any person under this section, whether\nor not a caution has been administered to him under subsection\n45(2) shall, whenever possible, be reduced into writing and signed\nby the person making it or affixed with his thumb-print, as the\ncase may be—\n\n(a) after it has been read to him in the language in which he\nmade it; and\n\n(b) after he has been given an opportunity to make any\ncorrection he may wish.\n\nStatement to be admissible in evidence"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A45","no":45,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 45"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"45. (1) Where any person is charged with an offence under this\nAct, any statement, whether the statement amounts to a confession\nor not or is oral or in writing, made at any time, whether before\nor after the person is charged and whether in the course of an\ninvestigation under this Act or not and whether or not wholly or\n\npartly in answer to questions, by that person to or in the hearing\nof an Assistant Controller or a police officer not below the rank\nof Inspector and whether or not interpreted to him by another\nAssistant Controller or police officer or other person shall,\nnotwithstanding any other written law to the contrary, be admissible\nin evidence at his trial and, if the person charged tenders himself\nas a witness, any such statement may be used in cross-examination\nand for the purpose of impeaching his credit.\n\n(2) The statement referred to in subsection (1)—\n(a) shall not be admissible or used under that subsection—\n\n(i) if the making of the statement appears to the court\nto have been caused by any inducement, threat or\npromise having reference to the charge proceeding\nfrom a person in authority and sufficient in the\nopinion of the court to give the person charged\ngrounds which would appear to him reasonable\nfor supposing that by making it he would gain any\nadvantage or avoid any evil of a temporal nature\nin reference to the proceeding against him; or\n\n(ii) in the case of a statement made by the person after\nhis arrest, unless the court is satisfied that a caution\nwas administered to him in the following words or\nwords to the like effect:\n\n\"It is my duty to warn you that you are not\nobliged to say anything or to answer any question,\nbut anything you say, whether in answer to a\nquestion or not, may be given in evidence.\";\nand\n\n(b) if made by any person before there is time to caution\nhim, shall not be rendered inadmissible in evidence merely\nby reason of no such caution having been administered\nif it has been administered as soon as possible.\n\n(3) Notwithstanding anything to the contrary contained in any\nwritten law, a person in respect of whom subsection (1) applies\nshall not be bound to answer any question relating to the case\nafter a caution under subsection (2) has been administered to him.\n\nOptical Discs                                            29\n\nForfeiture of articles, etc."}},{"id":"MY-H475-A46","no":46,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 46"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"46. (1) All articles, optical discs, things, books or documents\nseized in the exercise of any power conferred under this Act shall\nbe liable to forfeiture.\n\n(2) The court trying any person accused of an offence under\nthis Act may at the conclusion of the trial, whether he is convicted\nor not, order that the articles, optical discs, things, books or\ndocuments seized from that person be destroyed or, in the case of\ninfringing copies, be delivered up to the first owner of the copyright\nin question, or his assignee or exclusive licensee, as the case may\nbe.\n\n(3) Where there is no prosecution with regard to any article,\noptical disc, thing, book or document seized in exercise of any\npowers conferred under this Act, the article, optical disc, thing,\nbook or document shall be taken and deemed to be forfeited at\nthe expiration of one calendar month from the date it was seized\nunless a claim thereto is made before that date in the manner set\nout in subsection (4), (5) and (6).\n\n(4) Any person asserting that he is the owner of any article,\noptical disc, thing, book or document seized under this Act and\nthat the article, optical disc, thing, book or document is not liable\nto forfeiture may personally or by his agent authorised in writing\nby him give written notice to an Assistant Controller of his claim.\n\n(5) On receipt of a notice under subsection (4), the Assistant\nController shall refer the notice to the Controller who may, after\nsuch enquiry as may be necessary, direct that such article, optical\ndisc, thing, book or document be released or forfeited or refer the\nmatter to the Court of a First Class Magistrate for decision.\n\n(6) The court to which the matter is referred shall issue a\nsummons requiring the person asserting that he is the owner of\nthe article, optical disc, thing, book or document and the person\nfrom whom it was seized to appear before the court and upon\ntheir appearance or default to appear, due service of the summons\nbeing proved, the court shall proceed to the examination of the\nmatter, and on proof that an offence under this Act has been\ncommitted and that such article, optical disc, thing, book or\n\ndocument, was the subject-matter or was used in the commission\nof such offence, shall order the article, optical disc, thing, book\nor document to be forfeited or may, in the absence of such proof,\norder the release of such article, optical disc, thing, book or document\nto the person entitled to it.\n\n(7) Any article, optical disc, thing, book or document forfeited\nor deemed to be forfeited shall be delivered to the Controller who\nshall dispose of it in a manner he deems fit.\n\nCost of holding article, etc., seized"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A47","no":47,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 47"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"47. Where any article, optical disc, thing, book or document,\nseized under this Act is held in the custody of the Government\npending completion of any proceedings in respect of an offence\nunder this: iAct, the cost of holding such thing in custody shall, in\nthe event of any person being found guilty of an offence, be a\ndebt due to the Government by such person and shall be recoverable\naccordingly.\n\nNo costs or damages arising from seizure to be recoverable"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A48","no":48,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 48"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"48. No person shall, in any proceedings before any court in respect\nof any article, optical disc, thing, book or document seized in the\nexercise or the purported exercise of any power conferred under\nthis Act, be entitled to the costs of such proceedings or to any\ndamages or other relief unless such seizure was made without\nreasonable cause.\n\nProtection of informers"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A49","no":49,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 49"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"49. (1) Except as provided in this section, no witness in any\ncivil or criminal proceedings shall be obliged or permitted to\ndisclose the name or address of any informer or the substance and\nnature of the information received from him or to state any matter\nwhich may lead to his discovery.\n\n(2) If any book, document, record or paper which is in evidence\nor is liable to inspection in any civil or criminal proceedings\ncontains any entry in which any informer is named or described\nor which might lead to his discovery, the court shall cause all\nsuch entries to be concealed from view or to be obliterated so far\nonly as may be necessary to protect the informer from discovery.\n\nOptical Discs                                31\n\n(3) If in a trial for any offence under this Act the court after\nfull inquiry into the case believes that the informer wilfully made\nin his complaint a material statement which he knew or believed\nto be false or did not believe to be true, or if in any other proceeding\nthe court is of the opinion that justice cannot be fully done between\nthe parties to the proceeding without the discovery of the informer,\nit shall be lawful for the court to require the production of the\noriginal complaint, if in writing, and permit inquiry and require\nfull disclosure concerning the informer.\n\nReward for information"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A50","no":50,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 50"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VII"},"text":{"en":"50. In the case of a conviction involving a fine, the court imposing\nthe fine may, on the application of the prosecuting officer, direct\nthe payment of any part of the fine in such proportion as the court\nthinks fit but in any case not exceeding one half of such fine to\nthe person who gave the information leading to the conviction.\n\nPart VIII\n\nMISCELLANEOUS\n\nPower to exempt"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A51","no":51,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 51"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VIII"},"text":{"en":"51. (1) The Minister may by order published in the Gazette\nexempt, subject to such conditions as he may deem fit to impose,\nany person or class of persons or any business or class of businesses\nfrom all or any of the provision of this Act.\n\n(2) The Minister may, at any time by order published in the\nGazette, revoke any order made under subsection (1) if he is\nsatisfied that such exemption should no longer be granted.\n\nProtection of officers"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A52","no":52,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 52"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VIII"},"text":{"en":"52. No action or prosecution shall be brought, instituted or\nmaintained in any court against—\n\n(a) the Controller, a Deputy Controller, an Assistant Controller\nor any officer duly appointed under this Act or a police\nofficer for or on account of or in respect of any act\nordered or done for the purpose of carrying into effect\nthis Act; and\n\n(b) any other person for or an account of or in respect of\nany act done or purported to be done by him under the\norder, direction or instruction of the Controller, a Deputy\nController, an Assistant Controller or any officer duly\nappointed under this Act or a police officer if the act\nwas done in good faith and in a reasonable belief that it\nwas necessary for the purpose intended to be served\nthereby.\n\nInstitution of prosecution"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A53","no":53,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 53"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VIII"},"text":{"en":"53. No prosecution for or in relation to any offence under this\nAct shall be instituted except by or with the written consent of\nthe Public Prosecutor.\n\nJurisdiction to try offences"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A54","no":54,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 54"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VIII"},"text":{"en":"54. Notwithstanding any written law to the contrary, a court of\na Magistrate of the First Class shall have jurisdiction to try any\noffence under this Act and to impose the full punishment for any\nsuch offence.\n\nService of records, etc."}},{"id":"MY-H475-A55","no":55,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 55"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VIII"},"text":{"en":"55. (1) Records, other documents or information pertaining to\nthe manufacturing activity of any person required to be submitted\nor furnished or a notice given, a licence issued or a decision or\nan order made under this Act may be served personally or be sent\nby registered post.\n\n(2) Any record, other document or information, notice, licence,\ndecision or order which is sent by registered post shall be deemed\nto have been served on the person to whom it is addressed on the\nday succeeding the day on which the record, other document or\ninformation, notice, licence, decision or order would have been\nreceived in the ordinary course of post if it is addressed—\n\n(a) in the case of the Minister or the Controller, to either of\nthem, as the case may require, at the Ministry;\n\n(b) in the case of a company, a partnership or body of persons\nhaving a registered office in Malaysia, to that registered\n\n(c)\n\nOptical Discs                                       33\n\noffice or, where there is no such registered office, to the\ncompany's, partnership's or body's principal place of\nbusiness in Malaysia or, where there is no such principal\nplace of business, to the place where any other activity\nof the company, partnership or body is carried on; and\n\nin the case of an individual, to his last-known address.\n\nRegulations"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A56","no":56,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 56"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VIII"},"text":{"en":"56. (1)\n\nThe Minister may make such regulations as may be\n\nnecessary or expedient for giving full effect to the provisions of\n\nthis Act,\n\nfor carrying out or achieving the objects and purpose of\n\nthis Act, or for the further, better or more convenient implementation\nof the provision of this Act.\n\n(2) Without prejudice to the generality of subsection (1),\nregulations may be made—\n\n(a)\n\n(b)\n\n(c)\n\n(d)\n\n(e)\n\n(f)\n\nto prescribe the forms to be used and the information to\nbe furnished for any of the purposes of this Act;\n\nto prescribe the procedure for making applications for\nlicences and the determination of questions in connection\nwith the grant, surrender, suspension, renewal and\nrevocation of licences and the conditions to be attached\nto the licences and the procedure in connection with\nappeals;\n\nto prescribe the fees to be paid under this Act and the\nmanner for collecting and dealing with such fees;\n\nto prescribe the form of the register to be kept and\nmaintained by the Controller, the procedure and other\nmatters relating to the opening, maintenance and closure\nof the register and the procedure and other matters relating\nto the inspection of and taking of extracts from the register;\n\nto prescribe the form of records to be kept and maintained\nby the licensee and the information to be recorded and\nthe submission of such records; and\n\nto provide for any matter which under this Act is required\nor permitted to be prescribed or which is necessary or\nexpedient to be prescribed.\n\nSavings and transitional"}},{"id":"MY-H475-A57","no":57,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 57"},"chapter":{"en":"Part VIII"},"text":{"en":"57. (1) Any person engaged in the manufacturing of optical discs\nimmediately before the commencement of this Act and intends to\ncontinue to manufacture optical discs on and after such\ncommencement shall not later than six months from the date of\ncommencement of this Act apply to the Controller for a licence\nunder this Act.\n\n(2) Pending the decision by the Controller on the application\nfor a licence made under subsection (1), the applicant shall be\ndeemed to be licensed under this Act and no action shall be taken\nagainst him for engaging in the manufacture of optical discs without\na licence.\n\n(3) Where a licence is granted by the Controller under section\n7 pursuant to an application made under subsection (1), the applicant\nshall within six months from the date the licence is granted take\nthe necessary action to comply with the conditions imposed on\nthe licence.\n\n(4) Where a licence is not granted by the Controller under\nsection 7, the applicant referred to in subsection (2) shall cease\nto be deemed to be licensed under that subsection from the date\nhe is notified of the decision of the Controller or, if there is an\nappeal under section 18, the date of the decision of the Minister\non that appeal.\n\nSCHEDULE 1\n[Subsection 2(1)]\n\nLIST OF OPTICAL DISCS"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4750"] = {"id":"MY-H4750","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2021&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":6,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2021年所得税（豁免）（第9号）令","en":"INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 9) ORDER 2021","orig":"INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 9) ORDER 2021","ms":"Perintah Cukai Pendapatan (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 9) 2021","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế thu nhập (Miễn trừ) (số 9) năm 2021","th":"คำสั่งภาษีเงินได้ (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 9) ค.ศ. 2021","id":"Perintah Pajak Penghasilan (Pembebasan) (Nomor 9) Tahun 2021"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2021","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 6 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2021_P.U.(A)344-2021_INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 9) ORDER 2021.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4750-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini  bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Cukai Pendapatan\n(Pengecualian) (No. 9) 2021.\n\n (2) Perintah ini  berkuat kuasa mulai tahun taksiran 2021  hingga\ntahun taksiran 2022.\n\nTafsiran"}},{"id":"MY-H4750-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2.  Dalam Perintah ini—\n\n\"pelancong tempatan\" ertinya individu  warganegara Malaysia atau\nyang bermastautin di Malaysia;\n\n\"pelancong asing\" ertinya  individu selain daripada pelancong tempatan,\nyang bukan warganegara Malaysia atau yang tidak bermastautin di Malaysia; dan\n\n\"perniagaan pengendalian pelancongan \" mempunyai erti yang sama\nyang diberikan kepadanya dalam Akta Industri Pelancongan 1992 [Akta 482].\n\nOrang yang layak"}},{"id":"MY-H4750-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3.  Orang yang layak yang disebut dalam Perintah ini ialah suatu syarikat—\n\n(a) yang bermastautin di Malaysia;\n\n(b) yang dilesenkan di bawah Akta Industri Pelancongan 1992\nuntuk menjalankan suatu perniagaan pengendalian pelancongan; dan\n\n(c) yang menjalankan aktiviti yang layak.\n\nAktiviti yang layak"}},{"id":"MY-H4750-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. Aktiviti yang layak yang disebut dalam Perintah ini ialah suatu perniagaan\npengendalian pelancongan yang menyediakan suatu pakej pelancongan domestik\nbagi pengembaraan dalam Malaysia yang digunakan ole h pelancong  tempatan dan\npelancong asing, termasuk pengangkutan melalui udara, darat atau laut dan penginapan.\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H4750-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. (1)  Menteri mengecualikan orang yang layak  daripada pembayaran cukai\npendapatan dalam suatu tempoh asas bagi suatu tahun taksiran berkenaan dengan\npendapatan berkanun yang diperoleh daripada suatu aktiviti yang layak.\n\n (2)  Pengecualian yang diberikan di bawah  subperenggan (1) hendaklah\nhanya terpakai sekiranya jumlah bilangan pela ncong tempatan bagi ak tiviti yang layak\nitu tidak kurang daripada dua ratus  orang dalam suatu tempoh asas  bagi\nsuatu tahun taksiran.\n\n (3)  Jumlah bilangan pelancong tempatan dan pelancong asing bagi suatu\naktiviti yang layak  hendaklah ditentusahkan secara bertulis oleh seorang pegawai\nKementerian Pelancongan, Seni dan Budaya Malaysia yang diberi kuasa.\n\n  (4) Tiada apa -apa jua dalam subperenggan (1) boleh melepaskan atau\ndisifatkan telah melepaskan orang yang layak itu darip ada mematuhi apa-apa kehendak\nuntuk mengemukakan apa -apa penyata atau penyata akaun atau memberikan apa-apa\nmaklumat lain di bawah Akta.\n\nSumber berasingan dan akaun berasingan"}},{"id":"MY-H4750-A6","no":6,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 6"},"text":{"ms":"6. (1) Jika orang yang layak menjalankan suatu aktiviti yang layak dan suatu\naktiviti selain suatu aktiviti yang layak, setiap aktiviti hendaklah dikira sebagai suatu\nsumber berasingan dan berlainan bagi orang yang layak itu.\n\n (2) Orang yang layak yang diberikan pengecualian di bawah\nsubperenggan 5(1) hendaklah menyenggara suatu akaun yang berasingan bagi\npendapatan yang diperoleh daripada setiap aktiviti yang disebut dalam\nsubperenggan (1) dalam tempoh asas bagi setiap tahun taksiran.\n\nDibuat 15 Julai 2021\n[Perb.MOF.TAX(S)700-1/3/89; LHDN.AY.A.600-12/1/7(29)-139; PN(PU2)80/JLD.101]\n\nTENGKU DATUK SERI UTAMA ZAFRUL BIN TENGKU ABDUL AZIZ\nMenteri Kewangan\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut subsekyen 127(4)\nAkta Cukai Pendapatan 1967]\nINCOME TAX ACT 1967\n\nINCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 9) ORDER 2021\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 127(3) (b) of the\nIncome Tax Act 1967 [Act 53], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4751"] = {"id":"MY-H4751","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2022&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":5,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2022年联邦道路（私营管理）（通行费征收）（加影交通疏散环路）（修正）令","en":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KAJANG TRAFFIC DISPERSAL RING ROAD) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2022","orig":"FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KAJANG TRAFFIC DISPERSAL RING ROAD) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2022","ms":"Perintah Jalan Raya Persekutuan (Pengurusan Swasta) (Kutipan Tol) (Jalan Lingkaran Serakan Trafik Kajang) (Pindaan) 2022","vi":"Lệnh về Đường bộ liên bang (Quản lý tư nhân) (Thu phí đường bộ) (Đường vành đai phân tán giao thông Kajang) (Sửa đổi) năm 2022","th":"คำสั่งทางหลวงสหพันธ์ (การบริหารจัดการเอกชน) (การจัดเก็บค่าผ่านทาง) (ถนนวงแหวนกระจายการจราจรกาจัง) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2022","id":"Perintah Jalan Raya Federal (Pengelolaan Swasta) (Pemungutan Tol) (Jalan Lingkar Penyebaran Lalu Lintas Kajang) (Perubahan) Tahun 2022"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2022","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 5 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2022_P.U.(A)344-2022_FEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS) (KAJANG TRAFFIC DISPERSAL RING ROAD) (.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4751-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan\n\ntiga atau empat roda (tidak termasuk teksi\n\ndan bas)\n\n1.66"}},{"id":"MY-H4751-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan\n\nlima atau enam roda (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n3.60"}},{"id":"MY-H4751-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Kenderaan yang mempunyai tiga gandar atau\n\nlebih (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n5.40"}},{"id":"MY-H4751-A4","no":4,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 4"},"text":{"ms":"4. Teksi 0.83"}},{"id":"MY-H4751-A5","no":5,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 5"},"text":{"ms":"5. Bas 0.92\n\nBAHAGIAN II\n\nKADAR TOL BAGI TEMPOH DARI 1 JANUARI 2033 HINGGA 31 DISEMBER 2042\n\n(1)\n\nKelas Kenderaan\n\n(2)\n\nTol Kena Dibayar\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan\n\ntiga atau empat roda (tidak termasuk teksi\n\ndan bas)\n\n2.15\n\n2. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar dan\n\nlima atau enam roda (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n4.80\n\n3. Kenderaan yang mempunyai tiga gandar atau\n\nlebih (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n7.20\n\n4. Teksi 1.07\n\n5. Bas 1.19\n\nBAHAGIAN III\n\nKADAR TOL BAGI TEMPOH DARI 1 JANUARI 2043 HINGGA 31 JULAI 2062\n\n(1)\n\nKelas Kenderaan\n\n(2)\n\nTol Kena Dibayar\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar\n\ndan tiga atau empat roda (tidak termasuk\n\nteksi dan bas)\n\n2.30\n\n2. Kenderaan yang mempunyai dua gandar\n\ndan lima atau enam roda (tidak termasuk\n\nbas)\n\n4.80\n\n3. Kenderaan yang mempunyai tiga gandar\n\natau lebih (tidak termasuk bas)\n\n7.20\n\n4. Teksi 1.20\n\n5. Bas 1.54\n\nBagi maksud mengira bilangan gandar dan roda sesebuah kenderaan, gandar dan roda\n\nmana-mana treler yang ditarik oleh kenderaan itu hendaklah dikira sebagai sebahagian\n\ndaripada gandar dan roda kenderaan itu.\".\n\nDibuat 19 Oktober 2022\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/5; PN(PU2)426/LXIX]\n\n DATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\n Menteri Kanan Kerja Raya\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) ACT 1984\n\nFEDERAL ROADS (PRIVATE MANAGEMENT) (COLLECTION OF TOLLS)\n\n(KAJANG TRAFFIC DISPERSAL RING ROAD) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2022\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 2 of the Federal Roads\n\n(Private Management) Act 1984 [Act 306], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement\n\n1. (1) This order may be cited as the Federal Roads\n\n(Private Management) (Collection of Tolls) (Kajang Traffic Dispersal Ring Road)\n\n(Amendment) Order 2022.\n\n(2) This Order comes into operation on 20 October 2022.\n\nAmendment of paragraph 2\n\n2. The Federal Roads (Private Management) (Collection of Tolls)\n\n(Kajang Traffic Dispersal Ring Road) Order 2005 [P.U. (A) 16/2005], which is referred to\n\nas the \"principal Order\" in this Order, is amended in subparagraph 2(1)\n\nby substituting for the words \"1 August 2037\" the words \"31 July 2062\".\n\nSubstitution of First Schedule\n\n3. The principal Order is amended by substituting for the First Schedule\n\nthe following schedule:\n\n\"FIRST SCHEDULE\n\n[subparagraph 2(1)]\n\nPART I\n\nRATES OF TOLL FOR THE PERIOD FROM 20 OCTOBER 2022\n\nUNTIL 31 DECEMBER 2032\n\n(1)\n\nClasses of Vehicles\n\n(2)\n\nToll Payable\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Vehicles having two axles and three\n\nor four wheels (excluding taxis and buses)\n\n1.66\n\n2. Vehicles having two axles and five or\n\nsix wheels (excluding buses)\n\n3.60\n\n3. Vehicles having three axles or more\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n5.40\n\n4. Taxis 0.83\n\n5. Buses 0.92\n\nPART II\n\nRATES OF TOLL FOR THE PERIOD FROM 1 JANUARY 2033 UNTIL 31 DECEMBER 2042\n\n(1)\n\nClasses of Vehicles\n\n(2)\n\nToll Payable\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Vehicles having two axles and three\n\nor four wheels (excluding taxis and buses)\n\n2.15\n\n2. Vehicles having two axles and five or\n\nsix wheels (excluding buses)\n\n4.80\n\n3. Vehicles having three axles or more\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n7.20\n\n4. Taxis 1.07\n\n5. Buses 1.19\n\nPART III\n\nRATES OF TOLL FOR THE PERIOD FROM 1 JANUARY 2043 UNTIL 31 JULY 2062\n\n(1)\n\nClasses of Vehicles\n\n(2)\n\nToll Payable\n\n(RM)\n\n1. Vehicles having two axles and three or\n\nfour wheels (excluding taxis and buses)\n\n2.30\n\n2. Vehicles having two axles and five or\n\nsix wheels (excluding buses)\n\n4.80\n\n3. Vehicles having three axles or more\n\n(excluding buses)\n\n7.20\n\n4. Taxis 1.20\n\n5. Buses 1.54\n\nFor the purpose of calculating the number of axles and wheels of a vehicle,\n\nthe axles and wheels of any trailer towed by the vehicle shall be calculated as part\n\nof the axles and wheels of the vehicle.\".\n\nMade 19 October 2022\n\n[KKR.PUU.110-1/7/5; PN(PU2)426/LXIX]\n\n DATO' SRI HAJI FADILLAH BIN HAJI YUSOF\n\n Senior Minister of Works"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4752"] = {"id":"MY-H4752","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2023&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2023年所得税（豁免）（第4号）（2016年）（修正）令","en":"INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 4) 2016 (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2023","orig":"INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 4) 2016 (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2023","ms":"Perintah Cukai Pendapatan (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 4) (Tahun 2016) (Pindaan) 2023","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế thu nhập (Miễn trừ) (Số 4) (năm 2016) (Sửa đổi) năm 2023","th":"คำสั่งภาษีเงินได้ (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 4) (ค.ศ. 2016) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2023","id":"Perintah Pajak Penghasilan (Pembebasan) (Nomor 4) (Tahun 2016) (Perubahan) Tahun 2023"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2023","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2023_P.U.(A)344-2023_INCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 4) 2016 (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2023.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4752-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Cukai P endapatan (Pengecualian)\n(No. 4) 2016 (Pindaan) 2023.\n\nPindaan perenggan 6"}},{"id":"MY-H4752-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Perintah Cukai Pendapatan (Pengecualian) (No. 4) 2016 [ P.U. (A) 157/2016 ]\ndipinda dalam subperenggan 6(4) dengan menggantikan perkataan \"31 Disember 2022\"\ndengan perkataan \"31 Disember 2024\".\n\nDibuat 23 Oktober 2023\n[MOF.TAX(S)700-2/7/759; LHDN.AY.A 600-12/1(29)-182; PN(PU2)80/JLD.110]\n\n                                                                  ANWAR BIN IBRAHIM\n                                                                 Menteri Kewangan\n\n[Akan dibentangkan di Dewan Rakyat menurut subseksyen 127(4)\nAkta Cukai Pendapatan 1967]\nINCOME TAX ACT 1967\n\nINCOME TAX (EXEMPTION) (NO. 4) 2016 (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2023\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by paragraph 127(3)(b) of the Income Tax Act 1967\n[Act 53], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4753"] = {"id":"MY-H4753","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2024&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2024年印花税（豁免）（第3号）令","en":"STAMP DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 3) ORDER 2024","orig":"STAMP DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 3) ORDER 2024","ms":"Perintah Duti Setem (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 3) 2024","vi":"Lệnh về Thuế tem (Miễn trừ) (số 3) năm 2024","th":"คำสั่งอากรแสตมป์ (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 3) ค.ศ. 2024","id":"Perintah Bea Meterai (Pembebasan) (Nomor 3) Tahun 2024"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2024","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2024_P.U.(A)344-2024_STAMP DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 3) ORDER 2024.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4753-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1)  Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Duti Setem (Pengecualian)\n(No. 3) 2024.\n\n(2) Perintah ini disifatkan telah mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 Januari 2022.\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H4753-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. (1) Menteri mengecualikan surat cara perjanjian pinjaman atau pembiayaan\nbagi Kemudahan Pembiayaan Pelancongan PENJANA yang diluluskan di bawah\nDana Bank Negara Malaysia untuk Perusahaan Kecil dan Sederhana yang disempurnakan\nantara suatu institusi kewangan peserta dengan perusahaan kecil dan sederhana\ndaripada duti setem.\n\n(2) Pengecualian di bawah subperenggan (1) hendaklah—\n\n(a) hanya terpakai  bagi surat cara perjanjian pinjaman  atau\npembiayaan yang disempurnakan menurut suatu surat tawaran\nyang dikeluarkan oleh institusi kewangan peserta itu pada atau\nselepas 1 Januari 2022 tetapi tidak lewat dari 31 Disember 2023;                 dan\n\n(b) disertakan dengan suatu surat tawaran daripada institusi\nkewangan peserta kepada perusahaan kecil dan  sederhana\nyang menyatakan kelulusan kemudahan pinjaman atau\npembiayaan itu.\n\n(3) Dalam perenggan ini —\n\n(a) \"institusi kewangan peserta\" ertinya—\n\n(i) Affin Bank Berhad;\n\n(ii) Affin Islamic Bank Berhad;\n\n(iii) Alliance Bank Malaysia Berhad;\n\n(iv) Alliance Islamic Bank Berhad;\n\n(v) AmBank (M) Berhad;\n\n(vi) AmBank Islamic Berhad;\n\n(vii) Bank Islam Malaysia Berhad;\n\n(viii) Bank Simpanan Nasional;\n\n(ix) CIMB Bank Berhad;\n\n(x) CIMB Islamic Bank Berhad;\n\n(xi) Hong Leong Bank Berhad;\n\n(xii) Hong Leong Islamic Bank Berhad;\n\n(xiii) Malayan Banking Berhad;\n\n(xiv) Maybank Islamic Berhad;\n\n(xv) Bank Muamalat Malaysia Berhad;\n\n(xvi) Public Bank Berhad;\n\n(xvii) Public Islamic Bank Berhad;\n\n(xviii) RHB Bank Berhad;\n\n(xix) RHB Islamic Bank Berhad;\n\n(xx) Small Medium Enterprise Development Bank Malaysia\nBerhad (SME Bank);\n\n(b) \"perusahaan kecil dan sederhana\" mempunyai erti  yang diberikan\nkepadanya dalam seksyen 2  Akta Perbadanan Perusahaan Kecil\ndan Sederhana Malaysia 1995 [Akta 539].\n\nDibuat 12 November 2024\n[MOF.TAX.700-3/2/138; LHDN.AY.A 600-12/1/7(29)-324; PN(PU2)159/JLD.37]\n\nDATUK SERI AMIR HAMZAH BIN AZIZAN\nMenteri Kewangan II\n\nSTAMP ACT 1949\n\nSTAMP DUTY (EXEMPTION) (NO. 3) ORDER 2024\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 80(1) of the Stamp Act 1949\n[Act 378], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4754"] = {"id":"MY-H4754","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2025&status=PRINCIPAL","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2025年移民（豁免）（第2号）令","en":"IMMIGRATION (EXEMPTION) (NO. 2) ORDER 2025","orig":"IMMIGRATION (EXEMPTION) (NO. 2) ORDER 2025","ms":"Perintah Imigresen (Pengecualian) (Bilangan 2) 2025","vi":"Lệnh về Xuất nhập cảnh (Miễn trừ) (số 2) năm 2025","th":"คำสั่งการตรวจคนเข้าเมือง (การยกเว้น) (ฉบับที่ 2) ค.ศ. 2025","id":"Perintah Imigrasi (Pembebasan) (Nomor 2) Tahun 2025"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2025","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 3 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2025_P.U.(A)344-2025_IMMIGRATION (EXEMPTION) (NO. 2) ORDER 2025.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4754-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Imigresen (Pengecualian)\n\n(No. 2) 2025.\n\n(2) Perintah ini berkuat kuasa mulai 1 Oktober 2025 hingga 30 September 2026.\n\nPengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H4754-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Menteri mengecualikan mana-mana warganegara Singapura yang berikut\n\ndaripada pemakaian Pas yang sah yang dikeluarkan di bawah perenggan 6(1)(c) Akta:\n\n(a) pegawai Kerajaan Republik Singapura daripada Immigration and\n\nCheckpoints Authority, Singapore Police Force, Home Team Science and\n\nTechnology Agency dan Defence Science and Technology Agency\n\nyang terlibat dalam Projek Pembinaan Stesen Rapid Transit System\n\nLink di Bukit Chagar, Johor Bahru; dan\n\n(b) kontraktor atau subkontraktor yang diguna khidmat oleh\n\nKerajaan Republik Singapura bagi Projek Pembinaan Stesen Rapid Transit\n\nSystem Link di Bukit Chagar, Johor Bahru.\n\nSyarat pengecualian"}},{"id":"MY-H4754-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Mana-mana warganegara Singapura yang dikecualikan di bawah perenggan 2\n\nadalah tertakluk kepada syarat yang berikut:\n\n(a) kemasukan ke dalam Malaysia hendaklah melalui D11 Tambak Johor,\n\nJohor Bahru;\n\n(b) bagi setiap kemasukan ke dalam Malaysia ke tapak\n\nProjek Pembinaan Stesen Rapid Transit System Link\n\ndi Bukit Chagar, Johor Bahru, warganegara Singapura\n\nyang dikecualikan itu hendaklah mengemukakan maklumat\n\nyang dikehendaki kepada Agensi Kawalan dan Perlindungan\n\nSempadan Malaysia; dan\n\n(c) bagi setiap kemasukan ke dalam Malaysia, warganegara Singapura\n\nyang dikecualikan itu hanya dibenarkan untuk berada di Malaysia\n\nsecara sementara bagi tempoh tiga puluh hari.\n\nDibuat 29 September 2025\n\n[KDN.IM.S.600-2/1/11 JLD.18 (25); PN(PU2)100/JLD.18]\n\nDATUK SERI SAIFUDDIN NASUTION BIN ISMAIL\n\nMenteri Dalam Negeri\n\nIMMIGRATION ACT 1959/63\n\nIMMIGRATION (EXEMPTION) (NO. 2) ORDER 2025\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 55 of the Immigration Act 1959/63\n\n[Act 155], the Minister makes the following order:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4755"] = {"id":"MY-H4755","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 344/2026&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2026年国家技能发展（广告）（修正）条例","en":"NATIONAL SKILLS DEVELOPMENT (ADVERTISEMENT) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2026","orig":"NATIONAL SKILLS DEVELOPMENT (ADVERTISEMENT) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2026","ms":"Peraturan Pembangunan Kemahiran Kebangsaan (Iklan) (Pindaan) 2026","vi":"Quy định về Phát triển kỹ năng quốc gia (Quảng cáo) (Sửa đổi) năm 2026","th":"ข้อบังคับการพัฒนาทักษะแห่งชาติ (การโฆษณา) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2026","id":"Peraturan Pengembangan Keterampilan Nasional (Iklan) (Perubahan) Tahun 2026"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA344","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2026","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2026_P.U.(A)344-2026_NATIONAL SKILLS DEVELOPMENT (ADVERTISEMENT) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2026.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4755-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\n\nPembangunan Kemahiran Kebangsaan (Pengiklanan) (Pindaan) 2026.\n\n(2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 Oktober 2026.\n\nPindaan am"}},{"id":"MY-H4755-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Peraturan-Peraturan Pembangunan Kemahiran Kebangsaan (Pengiklanan) 2022\n\n[P.U. (A) 148/2022] dipinda dengan menggantikan perkataan \"atau program bertauliah\"\n\ndi mana-mana jua terdapat, termasuk dalam nota bahu, dengan perkataan \", program\n\nbertauliah atau Sijil\".\n\nDibuat 29 September 2026\n\n[KSM.PUU(S)600-1/2/16/2(27); PN(PU2)655/JLD.7]\n\nDATO' SRI RAMANAN RAMAKRISHNAN\n\nMenteri Sumber Manusia\n\nNATIONAL SKILLS DEVELOPMENT ACT 2006\n\nNATIONAL SKILLS DEVELOPMENT (ADVERTISEMENT) (AMENDMENT)\n\nREGULATIONS 2026\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 72 of the\n\nNational Skills Development Act 2006 [Act 652], the Minister makes the\n\nfollowing regulations:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4756"] = {"id":"MY-H4756","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 345/2000&status=PINDAAN","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2000年教育机构（纪律）（第一附表）（修正）令","en":"EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTIONS (DISCIPLINE) (FIRST SCHEDULE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2000","orig":"EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTIONS (DISCIPLINE) (FIRST SCHEDULE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2000","ms":"Perintah Institusi Pendidikan (Tatatertib) (Jadual Pertama) (Pindaan) 2000","vi":"Lệnh về Các cơ sở giáo dục (Kỷ luật) (Phụ lục thứ nhất) (Sửa đổi) năm 2000","th":"คำสั่งสถานศึกษา (วินัย) (ตารางผนวกที่หนึ่ง) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2000","id":"Perintah Institusi Pendidikan (Disiplin) (Lampiran Pertama) (Perubahan) Tahun 2000"},"level":"regulation","category":"05_其他及未分类","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA345","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2000","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\05_其他及未分类\\2000_P.U.(A)345-2000_EDUCATIONAL INSTITUTIONS (DISCIPLINE) (FIRST SCHEDULE) (AMENDMENT) ORDER 2000.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4756-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Perintah ini bolehlah dinamakan Perintah Institusi-Institusi Pelajaran\n(Tatatertib) (Jadual Pertama) (Pindaan) 2000.\n\n(2) Perintah ini hendaklah disifatkan telah mula berkuat kuasa pada 1 Januari\n\nP.U. (A) 345.                                  2622\n\nPindaan Jadual Pertama"}},{"id":"MY-H4756-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Jadual Pertama kepada Akta Institusi-Institusi Pelajaran (Tatatertib) 1976\ndipinda dalam butiran 29 dengan menggantikan perkataan \"Maktab Perguruan\nSeri Kota, Kuala Lumpur\" yang terdapat dalam ruang kedua dengan perkataan\n\"Institut Perguruan Bahasa-Bahasa Antarabangsa, Kuala Lumpur\".\n\nDibuat 15 April 2000.\n(KP(PUU)(S) 10075/07/10; PN(PU?)365]\n\nTan Sri Dato' Musa BIN MOHAMAD\nMenteri Pendidikan\n\nEDUCATIONAL INSTITUTIONS (DISCIPLINE) ACT 1976\n\nEDUCATIONAL INSTITUTIONS (DiscIPLINE) (First SCHEDULE)\n(AMENDMENT) Order 2000\n\nIn exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 22(2) of the Educational\nInstitutions (Discipline) Act 1976 [Act 174], the Minister makes the following\norder:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4757"] = {"id":"MY-H4757","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 345/2011&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":2,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2011年国民服务训练（责任的延期）（修正）条例","en":"NATIONAL SERVICE TRAINING (POSTPONEMENT OF LIABILITY) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2011","orig":"NATIONAL SERVICE TRAINING (POSTPONEMENT OF LIABILITY) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2011","ms":"Peraturan Latihan Khidmat Negara (Penangguhan Liabiliti) (Pindaan) 2011","vi":"Quy định về Huấn luyện Phục vụ Quốc gia (Hoãn nghĩa vụ) (Sửa đổi) năm 2011","th":"ข้อบังคับการฝึกบริการแห่งชาติ (การเลื่อนกำหนดความรับผิด) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2011","id":"Peraturan Pelatihan Dinas Nasional (Penundaan Kewajiban) (Perubahan) Tahun 2011"},"level":"regulation","category":"04_劳工与行政法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA345","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2011","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 2 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\04_劳工与行政法\\2011_P.U.(A)345-2011_NATIONAL SERVICE TRAINING (POSTPONEMENT OF LIABILITY) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2011.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4757-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\n\nLatihan Khidmat Negara (Penangguhan Tanggungan) (Pindaan) 2011.\n\n(2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 14 Oktober 2011.\n\nPindaan Jadual"}},{"id":"MY-H4757-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Peraturan-Peraturan Latihan Khidmat Negara (Penangguhan Tanggungan) 2004\n\n[P.U. (A) 26/2004] dipinda dengan menggantikan Borang 4 dalam Jadual dengan Borang\n\nyang berikut:\n\n\" Borang 4 (Form 4)\n\nJLKN/P/:04/Pin 1/11\n\n (NAMA PEMOHON PENANGGUHAN TANGGUNGAN)\n\n (NAME OF APPLICANT FOR POSPONEMENT OF LIABILITY)\n\n (ALAMAT)\n\n (ADDRESS)\n\n ……………………………………………….\n\n ……………………………………………….\n\n ……………………………………………….\n\n ……………………………………………….\n\n No. siri (Serial no.):\n\nAKTA LATIHAN KHIDMAT NEGARA 2003\n\n(NATIONAL SERVICE TRAINING ACT 2003)\n\nPERATURAN-PERATURAN LATIHAN KHIDMAT NEGARA\n\n(PENANGGUHAN TANGGUNGAN) 2004\n\n(NATIONAL SERVICE TRAINING (POSTPONEMENT OF LIABILITY)\n\nREGULATIONS 2004)\n\nPERAKUAN PENANGGUHAN\n\n(Peraturan 6)\n\n(POSTPONEMENT CERTIFICATION)\n\n(Regulation 6)\n\nDengan ini diperakukan bahawa (This is to certify that)\n\n ………..……………………………………….No.KP/NRICNo:…..………………………......................................\n\ntelah diberi penangguhan tanggungannya untuk menjalani latihan khidmat negara\n\nmulai (has been granted a postponement of liability to undergo national service\n\ntraining from)…………………………………….ke (to)………………………………………………………\n\nUntuk maklumat lanjut sila hubungi (For further enquiries please call):\n\n………………………\n\n…………………………………………………….\n\nKetua Pengarah\n\n (Director General) \".\n\nDibuat 27 September 2011\n\n[KP/JLKN(UPKN)(R)17/847/39 JIL 4; PN(PU2)635/IV]\n\n DATO' SERI DR AHMAD ZAHID BIN HAMIDI\n\n Menteri Pertahanan\n\nNATIONAL SERVICE TRAINING ACT 2003\n\nNATIONAL SERVICE TRAINING (POSTPONEMENT OF LIABILITY) (AMENDMENT)\n\nREGULATIONS 2011\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by section 20(5) of the National Service Training\n\nAct 2003 [Act 628], the Minister makes the following regulations:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
  FT["MY-H4758"] = {"id":"MY-H4758","coverage":"full","language":"ms","sourceName":"Attorney General's Chambers (AGC) Malaysia — Laws of Malaysia","sourceUrl":"https://lom.agc.gov.my/act-view.php?type=pua&no=P.U. (A) 345/2012&status=AMENDMENT","fetchedAt":"2026-10-28","articleCount":3,"structureMode":"ARTICLE","title":{"zh":"2012年货币服务业（最低资本金）（修正）条例","en":"MONEY SERVICES BUSINESS (MINIMUM CAPITAL FUNDS) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2012","orig":"MONEY SERVICES BUSINESS (MINIMUM CAPITAL FUNDS) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2012","ms":"Peraturan Perniagaan Perkhidmatan Wang (Dana Modal Minimum) (Pindaan) 2012","vi":"Quy định về Dịch vụ kinh doanh tiền tệ (Vốn tối thiểu) (Sửa đổi) năm 2012","th":"ข้อบังคับธุรกิจบริการเงินตรา (เงินทุนขั้นต่ำ) (การแก้ไข) ค.ศ. 2012","id":"Peraturan Usaha Jasa Keuangan (Dana Modal Minimum) (Perubahan) Tahun 2012"},"level":"regulation","category":"02_民商事与经济法","status":"active","docNumber":"PUA345","issuingBody":"马来西亚国会（Dewan Rakyat）","promulgatedDate":"2012","completenessNote":"全文：第 1 条至第 3 条；逐字未改写（源自厂商 OCR 文本）。原文马来文/英文双语并置，已分别落 text.ms 与 text.en。","textQuality":"ocr-vendor","sourceFile":"MY\\en\\TXT文本\\02_民商事与经济法\\2012_P.U.(A)345-2012_MONEY SERVICES BUSINESS (MINIMUM CAPITAL FUNDS) (AMENDMENT) REGULATIONS 2012.txt","country":"MY","countryName":"马来西亚","layer":"intl","articles":[{"id":"MY-H4758-A1","no":1,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 1"},"text":{"ms":"1. (1) Peraturan-peraturan ini bolehlah dinamakan Peraturan-Peraturan\nPerniagaan Perkhidmatan Wang (Dana Modal Minimum) (Pindaan) 2012.\n\n (2) Peraturan-Peraturan ini mula berkuat kuasa pada 25 Oktober 2012.\n\nPindaan peraturan 2"}},{"id":"MY-H4758-A2","no":2,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 2"},"text":{"ms":"2. Peraturan-Peraturan Perniagaan Perkhidmatan  Wang (Dana Modal Minimum)\n2011 [ P.U. (A) 392/2011 ] yang disebut \"Peraturan -Peraturan ibu\" dalam\nPeraturan-Peraturan ini, dipinda dalam peraturan 2 dengan memotong takrif\n\"nilai perolehan tahunan\".\n\nPindaan Jadual"}},{"id":"MY-H4758-A3","no":3,"noLabel":{"en":"Section 3"},"text":{"ms":"3. Jadual kepada Peraturan -Peraturan ibu dipinda berkenaan dengan Golongan B\natau C, dengan menggantikan butir-butir dalam ruang \"Kriteria\" dan ruang \"Dana modal\nminimum (RM)\" dengan butir-butir yang berikut:\n\"\nGolongan Kriteria Dana modal\nminimum (RM)\nB atau C Pemegang lesen menjalankan perniagaan\npengurupan wang atau perniagaan\npengiriman wang dengan lebih daripada lima\npejabat cawangan.\n\n2,000,000\n\nGolongan Kriteria Dana modal\nminimum (RM)\nPemegang lesen menjalankan perniagaan\npengurupan wang atau perniagaan\npengiriman wang, jika—\n\n(a) ia juga adalah ejen perniagaan\nperkhidmatan wang kepada  seorang\npemegang lesen kepada suatu\ngolongan yang berbeza; atau\n\n(b) ia mempunyai sehingga lima pejabat\ncawangan.\n\n500,000\nPemegang lesen menjalankan perniagaan\npengurupan wang atau perniagaan\npengiriman wang tanpa pejabat cawangan.\n\n300,000\n\".\n\nDibuat 17 Oktober 2012\n[BNM.JUN. 1119/67/03; PN(PU2)701/II]\n\nDATO' SRI MOHD NAJIB BIN TUN ABDUL RAZAK\nMenteri Kewangan\n\nMONEY SERVICES BUSINESS ACT 2011\n\nMONEY SERVICES BUSINESS (MINIMUM CAPITAL FUNDS) (AMENDMENT)\nREGULATIONS 2012\n\nIN exercise of the powers conferred by subsection 22(1) of the Money Services Business\nAct 2011 [ Act 731 ], the Minister, on the recommendation of the Bank, makes the\nfollowing regulations:\n\nCitation and commencement"}}],"pack":"my-10"};
